const e="tiantiandu-2b",n="自行车王国",i="Bicycle Kingdom",t="中文天天读",h="Reading China",o="2B",a=[{n:1,title:"盲人的灯笼",py:"Mángrén de dēnglong",en:"The Blindman's Lantern",chars:130,daodu:"帮助别人，也是帮助自己。如果你经常帮助别人，当你需要帮助的时候，别人也会帮助你。",daoduEn:"Helping others is also helping yourself. If you often help other people, then when you need help, they will help you too.",paras:[{zh:"有一个盲人，他每次晚上出去的时候，手里总是提着一个明亮的灯笼。别人看了觉得很奇怪，就问他：“你自己看不见，为什么还要提着灯笼走路呢？”",py:"Yǒu yí gè mángrén, tā měi cì wǎnshang chūqù de shíhou, shǒu li zǒngshì tízhe yí gè míngliàng de dēnglong. Biérén kànle juéde hěn qíguài, jiù wèn tā: “Nǐ zìjǐ kànbujiàn, wèishénme hái yào tízhe dēnglong zǒulù ne?”",en:`There was a blind man who always carried a bright lantern whenever he went out at night. People found this very strange, so they asked him, "You can't see anything yourself, so why do you carry a lantern when you walk?"`},{zh:"盲人笑着说：“我自己看不见，但是，我的灯笼可以照亮别人呀。”",py:"Mángrén xiàozhe shuō: “Wǒ zìjǐ kànbujiàn, dànshì, wǒ de dēnglong kěyǐ zhàoliàng biérén ya.”",en:`The blind man smiled and said, "I can't see, but my lantern can light the way for other people."`},{zh:"“照亮别人，跟你有什么关系呢？”",py:"“Zhàoliàng biérén, gēn nǐ yǒu shénme guānxi ne?”",en:'"Lighting the way for others — what does that have to do with you?"'},{zh:"盲人说：“我提着灯笼不是为自己照路，而是为了让别人看到我。这样，他们就不会撞到我了。”",py:"Mángrén shuō: “Wǒ tízhe dēnglong bú shì wèi zìjǐ zhàolù, ér shì wèile ràng biérén kàndào wǒ. Zhèyàng, tāmen jiù bú huì zhuàngdào wǒ le.”",en:`The blind man said, "I don't carry the lantern to light my own way. I carry it so that other people can see me. That way, they won't bump into me."`}],vocab:[{w:"盲人",py:"mángrén",pos:"n.",en:"blindman"},{w:"提",py:"tí",pos:"v.",en:"carry"},{w:"明亮",py:"míngliàng",pos:"adj.",en:"bright"},{w:"灯笼",py:"dēnglong",pos:"n.",en:"lantern"},{w:"奇怪",py:"qíguài",pos:"adj.",en:"weird"},{w:"照亮",py:"zhàoliàng",pos:"",en:"light"},{w:"撞",py:"zhuàng",pos:"v.",en:"bump into"}],points:[{name:"跟……（没）有关系",en:"have something/nothing to do with",eg:"照亮别人，跟你有什么关系呢？",egEn:"Does lighting the way for others do anything for you?",zh:"“A跟B（没）有关系”中“关系”是名词，表示人或事物之间的某种联系。如果A和B之间有联系，就说“A跟B有关系”，否定则说“A跟B没有关系”。",enx:"In the phrase “A跟B（没）有关系”, “关系” is a noun to show the relationship between people or things. If A has something to do with B, we say “A跟B有关系”. Otherwise, we say “A跟B没有关系”.",egs:["（1）我今天迟到，跟昨天睡觉晚有很大关系。","（2）考试成绩跟学习时间、学习兴趣有很大关系。"]},{name:"就",en:"exactly, precisely",eg:"这样，他们就不会撞到我了。",egEn:"In this way, they will not bump into me.",zh:"“就”，副词。表示承接上文情况，得出结论。",enx:"“就” is an adverb that introduces a conclusion on the basis of the previous sentence(s).",egs:["（1）没事儿就回家吧，好好休息休息。","（2）有他参加就好，我最喜欢听他唱歌了。"]}],think:["那个盲人为什么要提灯笼？","你觉得那个盲人聪明不聪明？为什么？"],tf:[{q:"那个盲人很奇怪，因为他总是在白天提着灯笼。",a:!1},{q:"那个盲人提灯笼，是怕别人看不见路。",a:!1},{q:"盲人每天晚上都提灯笼出去。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"中国人的红灯笼",titleEn:"Red Lanterns of the Chinese",zh:"盲人的“灯笼”是用来照路的。不过在中国，灯笼除了照明之外，还有很多其他的含义。早在汉朝，每年的元宵节前后，家家户户就挂起红灯笼，以此营造红火、喜庆的气氛。后来，红灯笼就成了团圆、兴旺、富贵的象征。喜庆的日子，人们都喜欢挂起红红的灯笼。尤其是在海外华人聚居区，比如唐人街，一年四季都挂着大红灯笼。",en:"The blindman's “lantern” was used to light his way. However, apart from lighting the way, lanterns in China have many uses. As early as the Han Dynasty, households hung red lanterns during the Lantern Festival to create an atmosphere of lively festivity. Later, red lanterns have gradually become the token of reunion, prosperity and wealth, dignity and fortune. On festive occasions, people usually hang red lanterns. Particularly in the overseas Chinese residential areas, like China towns, lanterns are hung all the year around."}},{n:2,title:"汉语的发音有点儿难",py:"Hànyǔ de fāyīn yǒudiǎnr nán",en:"Pronouncing Chinese Is a Little Difficult",chars:208,daodu:"现在越来越多的外国人开始学习汉语。有的人觉得汉语的发音很难。你觉得呢？",daoduEn:"More and more foreigners are starting to learn Chinese. Some find Chinese pronunciation very hard. What do you think?",paras:[{zh:"汉语的发音有点儿难。为什么呢？",py:"Hànyǔ de fāyīn yǒudiǎnr nán. Wèishénme ne?",en:"Chinese pronunciation is a little difficult. Why?"},{zh:"第一，因为汉语有四个声调。外国人觉得声调很难，经常闹笑话。一次，一个外国人找不到他要去的那家超市。他看见旁边有一位漂亮的女士，就说：“小姐，我有一个问题，我能问你吗？”那位女士听了却非常生气。你知道为什么吗？因为那个外国人把“wèn（问）”说成了“wěn（吻）”。除了声调以外，儿化音也不容易。比如说，“小孩”要说成“小孩儿”。",py:"Dì-yī, yīnwèi Hànyǔ yǒu sì gè shēngdiào. Wàiguórén juéde shēngdiào hěn nán, jīngcháng nào xiàohua. Yí cì, yí gè wàiguórén zhǎo bú dào tā yào qù de nà jiā chāoshì. Tā kànjiàn pángbiān yǒu yí wèi piàoliang de nǚshì, jiù shuō: “Xiǎojiě, wǒ yǒu yí gè wèntí, wǒ néng wèn nǐ ma?” Nà wèi nǚshì tīngle què fēicháng shēngqì. Nǐ zhīdào wèishénme ma? Yīnwèi nàge wàiguórén bǎ “wèn” shuōchéngle “wěn”. Chúle shēngdiào yǐwài, érhuàyīn yě bù róngyì. Bǐrúshuō, “xiǎohái” yào shuōchéng “xiǎoháir”.",en:`First, because Chinese has four tones. Foreigners find the tones very hard and often make funny mistakes. Once, a foreigner couldn't find the supermarket he was looking for. He saw a pretty lady nearby and said, "Miss, I have a question. May I ask you?" But when the lady heard this, she got very angry. Do you know why? Because he said "wěn" (吻, to kiss) instead of "wèn" (问, to ask) — so it sounded like "May I kiss you?" Besides the tones, the "-r" ending isn't easy either. For example, "xiǎohái" (child) should be said as "xiǎoháir".`},{zh:"第二，卷舌音很难。比如说，“我是（shì）美国人”，有的留学生说成“我是（sì）美国人”。还有，“四”和“十”很多人也分不清楚。所以上课的时候，老师让我们说：四是四，十是十；十四是十四，四十是四十。",py:"Dì-èr, juǎnshéyīn hěn nán. Bǐrúshuō, “wǒ shì Měiguórén”, yǒude liúxuéshēng shuōchéng “wǒ sì Měiguórén”. Háiyǒu, “sì” hé “shí” hěn duō rén yě fēn bù qīngchu. Suǒyǐ shàngkè de shíhou, lǎoshī ràng wǒmen shuō: sì shì sì, shí shì shí; shísì shì shísì, sìshí shì sìshí.",en:`Second, sounds made with a curled tongue are hard. For example, some foreign students say "Wǒ sì Měiguórén" instead of "Wǒ shì Měiguórén" (I am American). Also, lots of people can't tell "four" (sì) from "ten" (shí). So in class, our teacher makes us say: "Sì shì sì, shí shì shí; shísì shì shísì, sìshí shì sìshí" — four is four, ten is ten; fourteen is fourteen, forty is forty.`}],vocab:[{w:"声调",py:"shēngdiào",pos:"n.",en:"tone"},{w:"超市",py:"chāoshì",pos:"n.",en:"supermarket"},{w:"女士",py:"nǚshì",pos:"n.",en:"lady"},{w:"生气",py:"shēngqì",pos:"v.",en:"get angry"},{w:"吻",py:"wěn",pos:"v.",en:"kiss"},{w:"除了",py:"chúle",pos:"",en:"apart from"},{w:"卷舌音",py:"juǎnshéyīn",pos:"n.",en:"curling of the tongue (retroflex)"},{w:"分",py:"fēn",pos:"v.",en:"distinguish"},{w:"清楚",py:"qīngchu",pos:"adj.",en:"clear"}],points:[{name:"闹笑话",en:"make a fool of oneself",eg:"外国人觉得声调很难，经常闹笑话。",egEn:"Non-Chinese speakers feel it is difficult to learn tones, and sometimes make fools of themselves.",zh:"“闹笑话”是指因粗心大意或缺乏知识经验而发生可笑的错误。",enx:"“闹笑话” means “to make a fool of oneself because of carelessness or lack of knowledge and experience”.",egs:["（1）不懂广东话的人刚到广东，常常会闹笑话。","（2）我刚来中国的时候，闹了不少笑话。"]},{name:"比如说",en:"for example",eg:"卷舌音很难。比如说，“我是（shì）美国人”，有的留学生说成“我是（sì）美国人”。",egEn:"Curling of the tongue (retroflex) is difficult. For example, some foreign students say “我是（sì）美国人” instead of “我是（shì）美国人”.",zh:"“比如说”，用来引出说明某事物、某情况的例子。",enx:"The phrase “比如说” is used to introduce an example to illustrate something or some circumstances.",egs:["（1）中国菜有很多种，比如说，四川菜、广东菜、山东菜，种类不一样，口味也不一样。","（2）我们班的同学来自很多不同的国家，比如说，日本、美国和英国。"]}],think:["汉语有几个声调？","那位女士为什么很生气？","你觉得“四”和“十”的发音容易吗？"],tf:[{q:"汉语有三个声调。",a:!1},{q:"外国人觉得汉语的声调很难，儿化音很容易。",a:!1},{q:"女士听了外国人的话很生气，因为她不想帮助他。",a:!1},{q:"外国人说“四”和“十”时，发音可能是一样的。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"汉语的声调",titleEn:"Chinese Tones",zh:`汉语是有声调的语言，声调不同，意思就不同，因此，声调具有区别意义的作用。比如，mā（妈）、má（麻）、mǎ（马）、mà（骂）。
不同声调连在一起时，有时会出现变调。两个第三声的音节连在一起时，前一个音节变为第二声。比如，“你好（nǐhǎo）”的实际读音为“níhǎo”。`,en:"Chinese is a tonal language. Different tones produce different meanings. Thus, tones can be used to distinguish between meanings, such as mā (妈, mother), má (麻, hemp), mǎ (马, horse), mà (骂, curse). Changes in tone may result in different tone combinations. When two characters in the third tone are put together, the first character changes into the second tone. For example, “你好（nǐhǎo）” is pronounced as “níhǎo”."}},{n:3,title:"好",py:"Hǎo",en:"Good",chars:211,daodu:"你想过吗，“女”和“子”在一起，为什么就组成（zǔchéng: compose）了“好”字？你是怎么记住汉字的？",daoduEn:"Have you ever wondered why 女 (woman) and 子 (child) put together make the character 好 (good)? How do you remember Chinese characters?",paras:[{name:"张老师",zh:"同学们好！我是你们的汉语老师，我的名字叫“张好”。",py:"Tóngxuémen hǎo! Wǒ shì nǐmen de Hànyǔ lǎoshī, wǒ de míngzi jiào “Zhāng Hǎo”.",en:`Hello, everyone! I'm your Chinese teacher. My name is Zhang Hao — "Hǎo" as in 好, "good".`},{name:"学生们",zh:"老师好！",py:"Lǎoshī hǎo!",en:"Hello, teacher!"},{name:"张老师",zh:"老师的名字是什么意思，你们知道吗？",py:"Lǎoshī de míngzi shì shénme yìsi, nǐmen zhīdào ma?",en:"Do you know what my name means?"},{name:"学生甲",zh:"知道。张老师是个“好”老师。",py:"Zhīdào. Zhāng lǎoshī shì gè “hǎo” lǎoshī.",en:'Yes. It means Teacher Zhang is a "good" (hǎo) teacher!'},{name:"张老师",zh:"谢谢！我会加油的。大家想一想，为什么“好”这个字是“女”和“子”在一起呀？",py:"Xièxie! Wǒ huì jiāyóu de. Dàjiā xiǎng yì xiǎng, wèishénme “hǎo” zhège zì shì “nǚ” hé “zǐ” zài yìqǐ ya?",en:"Thank you! I'll do my best. Now, everyone, think about this: why is the character 好 (good) made of 女 (woman) and 子 (child)?"},{name:"学生乙",zh:"“女子”就是女孩子，有了女朋友就是“好”。",py:"“Nǚzǐ” jiù shì nǚháizi, yǒule nǚpéngyou jiù shì “hǎo”.",en:`"女子" means a girl — when you've got a girlfriend, life is "good"!`},{name:"学生丙",zh:"不对。“女”是“女儿”，“子”是“儿子”，又有女儿又有儿子就是“好”。",py:"Bú duì. “Nǚ” shì “nǚ'ér”, “zǐ” shì “érzi”, yòu yǒu nǚ'ér yòu yǒu érzi jiù shì “hǎo”.",en:`No, that's not it. 女 means "daughter" and 子 means "son". Having both a daughter and a son — that's "good"!`},{name:"学生丁",zh:"也不对。“女”是“女孩儿”，“子”是“男孩儿”，女孩儿和男孩儿在一起就是“好”。我们班女孩儿、男孩儿一起学汉语，很好！",py:"Yě bú duì. “Nǚ” shì “nǚháir”, “zǐ” shì “nánháir”, nǚháir hé nánháir zài yìqǐ jiù shì “hǎo”. Wǒmen bān nǚháir, nánháir yìqǐ xué Hànyǔ, hěn hǎo!",en:`That's not it either. 女 means "girl" and 子 means "boy". Girls and boys together — that's "good"! In our class, girls and boys learn Chinese together. Very good!`},{name:"张老师",zh:"同学们说得都很有意思。以后你们学习汉字的时候多想一想，就容易记住了。",py:"Tóngxuémen shuō de dōu hěn yǒuyìsi. Yǐhòu nǐmen xuéxí Hànzì de shíhou duō xiǎng yì xiǎng, jiù róngyì jìzhù le.",en:"Your ideas are all very interesting. From now on, when you learn Chinese characters, think about them a bit more, and they'll be easy to remember."}],vocab:[{w:"意思",py:"yìsi",pos:"n.",en:"meaning"},{w:"加油",py:"jiāyóu",pos:"v.",en:"do one's best"},{w:"有意思",py:"yǒuyìsi",pos:"adj.",en:"interesting"},{w:"以后",py:"yǐhòu",pos:"n.",en:"from now on"},{w:"记住",py:"jìzhù",pos:"v.",en:"memorize"}],points:[{name:"一起",en:"together, in the same place",eg:"女孩儿和男孩儿在一起就是“好”。",egEn:"It is nice (好) for girls (女) and boys (子) to stay together.",zh:"“一起”可以作名词。表示“同一处所”或“一块儿”的意思。“一起”也可以作副词。表示动作行为发生在同一地点或合在一处。",enx:"“一起” is a noun that means “in the same place” or “together”. It can also be used as an adverb to indicate “actions taking place in the same place or at the same time”.",egs:["（1）你们两个站在一起，让我看看谁高一点儿。","（2）我们两个人一起学习了四年，现在是很好的朋友。"]},{name:"容易",en:"easy, likely",eg:"以后你们学习汉字的时候要多想一想，就容易记住了。",egEn:"Think more when learning Chinese characters and you will memorize them easily.",zh:"“容易”，形容词。表示发生某种变化的可能性较大。",enx:"“容易” is an adjective that indicates “a high degree of probability”.",egs:["（1）留学生在中国很容易学好汉语。","（2）常常运动的人不容易生病。"]}],think:["“好”字为什么是“女”和“子”在一起，同学们说出了几种答案？都是什么？","你学过的汉字中，哪些像“好”一样，是两个字的？说说它们的意思。"],tf:[{q:"张老师叫张好，“好”是名字。",a:!0},{q:"名字里有“好”的老师都是好老师。",a:!1},{q:"“女子”是女朋友的意思。",a:!1},{q:"“子”是女孩儿的意思。",a:!1},{q:"多想想汉字的意思，就容易记住汉字。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"会意字",titleEn:"Associative Compounds",zh:"会意是汉字的一种造字法，就是把两个或两个以上的独体字根据意义之间的关系合成一个字，表示两者合成的意义。有的会意字由不同的字组成，如本文中的“好”就是由“女”和“子”组成的。关于“好”字有几种说法，有的认为女子有了孩子，是件好事，还有的认为指女子貌美。“武”也是个会意字，由“戈”和“止”组成，表示人拿着武器走。有的会意字由相同的字组成。如“从”，表示两人前后相随。随着语言的发展，一些会意字还沿用原来的意思，如“从”，但有的意思已有了很大改变，如“好”。",en:"One of the Chinese character formation methods is associative compound. That is to say, two or more single-component characters are combined together to form a compound character with their associative meanings. Some associative compounds consist of different characters. For example, in our text “好” is formed with “女” and “子”. There are different interpretations of the origins of the character “好”. Some believe that the character indicates that it is nice for a woman to have a child, while others assume its original meaning is “beauty of a lady”. Another example is the character “武(wǔ)”, consisting of “戈(gē)” and “止(zhǐ)” with the implication of a man walking with a weapon in hand. Some associative compounds are formed with the same characters, like “从”. It suggests one person follows the other. With the development of the language, people continue to use the original meanings of some associative compounds, like “从”; however, some other compounds have undergone great changes in their meaning, like “好”."}},{n:4,title:"穷和尚和富和尚",py:"Qióng héshang hé fù héshang",en:"Poor Monk, Rich Monk",chars:160,daodu:"“做”永远比“说”好，路就在脚下！",daoduEn:"Doing is always better than talking. The road starts right under your feet!",paras:[{zh:"从前有两个和尚，一个很有钱，另一个很穷。",py:"Cóngqián yǒu liǎng gè héshang, yí gè hěn yǒuqián, lìng yí gè hěn qióng.",en:"Long ago there were two monks. One was very rich, and the other was very poor."},{zh:"有一天，穷和尚对富和尚说：“我想到印度去学习佛经，你觉得怎么样？”",py:"Yǒu yì tiān, qióng héshang duì fù héshang shuō: “Wǒ xiǎng dào Yìndù qù xuéxí fójīng, nǐ juéde zěnmeyàng?”",en:`One day, the poor monk said to the rich monk, "I'm thinking of going to India to study the Buddhist scriptures. What do you think?"`},{zh:"富和尚说：“路太远了，你怎么去呢？”",py:"Fù héshang shuō: “Lù tài yuǎn le, nǐ zěnme qù ne?”",en:`The rich monk said, "It's a very long way. How will you get there?"`},{zh:"穷和尚说：“我有一个碗、一个杯子和一双脚，够了吧。”",py:"Qióng héshang shuō: “Wǒ yǒu yí gè wǎn, yí gè bēizi hé yì shuāng jiǎo, gòu le ba.”",en:'The poor monk said, "I have a bowl, a cup and a pair of feet. That should be enough, right?"'},{zh:"富和尚听了以后，大笑说：“我想去印度已经有好多年了，可一直都没有去，就是因为我的钱不够。你那么穷，怎么去得了呢？”",py:"Fù héshang tīngle yǐhòu, dà xiào shuō: “Wǒ xiǎng qù Yìndù yǐjīng yǒu hǎo duō nián le, kě yìzhí dōu méiyǒu qù, jiù shì yīnwèi wǒ de qián bú gòu. Nǐ nàme qióng, zěnme qù de liǎo ne?”",en:`The rich monk laughed out loud and said, "I've wanted to go to India for many years, but I've never gone — simply because I don't have enough money. You're so poor, how could you ever make it there?"`},{zh:"三年以后，穷和尚从印度回来了，还带了一本佛经送给了富和尚。富和尚非常不好意思。",py:"Sān nián yǐhòu, qióng héshang cóng Yìndù huílái le, hái dàile yì běn fójīng sònggěile fù héshang. Fù héshang fēicháng bùhǎoyìsi.",en:"Three years later, the poor monk came back from India, and he even brought a Buddhist scripture as a gift for the rich monk. The rich monk felt very embarrassed."}],vocab:[{w:"和尚",py:"héshang",pos:"n.",en:"monk"},{w:"穷",py:"qióng",pos:"adj.",en:"poor"},{w:"富",py:"fù",pos:"adj.",en:"rich"},{w:"印度",py:"Yìndù",pos:"n.",en:"India"},{w:"佛经",py:"fójīng",pos:"n.",en:"Buddhist scripture"},{w:"碗",py:"wǎn",pos:"n.",en:"bowl"},{w:"脚",py:"jiǎo",pos:"n.",en:"foot"},{w:"够",py:"gòu",pos:"v.",en:"be enough, suffice"}],points:[{name:"去得了",en:"be able to go",eg:"你那么穷，怎么去得了呢？",egEn:"You are that poor, how can you manage to go there?",zh:"“去得了”，动词后接可能补语。“动词+得了”表示“能+动词”；“动词+不了”表示“不能+动词”。",enx:"The structure of “去得了” is “v. + complement”, and it indicates “the possibility of doing something”. “v.得了” means “能v.”, while “v.不了” indicates “不能v.”.",egs:["（1）那儿太远了，走路去不了。","（2）一个西瓜 10 块钱，我有 20 块，买得了。"]},{name:"不好意思",en:"feel shy/ashamed",eg:"富和尚非常不好意思。",egEn:"The rich monk felt very ashamed.",zh:"“不好意思”表示“害羞”、“惭愧”的意思。",enx:"“不好意思” means “shy”, “ashamed”.",egs:["（1）他才考了 70 分，觉得很不好意思。","（2）大家都说她很漂亮，她觉得挺不好意思的。"]}],think:["听了穷和尚的话，富和尚为什么大笑？","穷和尚说“一个碗、一个杯子和一双脚”就够了，为什么？","富和尚为什么不好意思？"],tf:[{q:"两个和尚都没有钱。",a:!1},{q:"穷和尚想让富和尚跟他一起去印度。",a:!1},{q:"穷和尚去印度是为了玩儿。",a:!1},{q:"富和尚觉得钱不够不可能去印度。",a:!0},{q:"富和尚没想过去印度。",a:!1},{q:"穷和尚最后成功（chénggōng：successful）地去了印度。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"佛教在中国",titleEn:"Buddhism in China",zh:"佛教是与基督教、伊斯兰教并列的世界三大宗教之一。公元前六世纪至公元前五世纪，佛教由释迦牟尼创建于古印度，并开始向境外传播。据记载，西汉时期佛教传入中国。在漫长的历史过程中，佛教在中国已远远超出了宗教范围，逐渐渗透到中国文化的各个领域，包括语言文字、哲学思想、史学艺术、科技建筑、乃至民风民俗，成为中国传统文化的重要组成部分。",en:"Buddhism is one of the three most influential religions in the world, together with Christianity and Islam. It was established by Sakyamuni in ancient India from the 6th century BC to the 5th century BC, and then began to spread abroad. It is recorded that Buddhism was introduced into China in the Western Han Dynasty. Buddhism is much more than a religious belief in China after its long evolution, and has gradually penetrated into all aspects of Chinese culture, like language, philosophical ideology, history, arts, science, architecture, and even folk customs. Consequently, it has become an important part of traditional Chinese culture."}},{n:5,title:"砍价",py:"Kǎnjià",en:"Bargaining",chars:208,daodu:"你在中国砍过价吗？如果你会砍价，就能买到便宜的东西。",daoduEn:"Have you ever bargained in China? If you know how to bargain, you can buy things cheap.",paras:[{zh:"我是外国留学生。我发现在中国买东西很特别，那就是可以砍价。砍价才能买到便宜的东西。砍价有五步：“我喜欢”，“多少钱”，“太贵了”，“我走了”，“OK了”。下面是我昨天买东西砍价的对话。",py:"Wǒ shì wàiguó liúxuéshēng. Wǒ fāxiàn zài Zhōngguó mǎi dōngxi hěn tèbié, nà jiù shì kěyǐ kǎnjià. Kǎnjià cái néng mǎidào piányi de dōngxi. Kǎnjià yǒu wǔ bù: “wǒ xǐhuan”, “duōshao qián”, “tài guì le”, “wǒ zǒu le”, “OK le”. Xiàmiàn shì wǒ zuótiān mǎi dōngxi kǎnjià de duìhuà.",en:`I'm a foreign student. I've found that shopping in China is special: you can bargain. Only by bargaining can you get things cheap. Bargaining has five steps: "I like it," "How much?", "Too expensive!", "I'm leaving," and "OK!" Here's the conversation I had while bargaining yesterday.`},{name:"老板",zh:"这件衣服很漂亮，试试吧！",py:"Zhè jiàn yīfu hěn piàoliang, shìshi ba!",en:"This is a really nice piece of clothing. Try it on!"},{name:"我",zh:"多少钱？",py:"Duōshao qián?",en:"How much?"},{name:"老板",zh:"不贵，一百六十块。",py:"Bú guì, yìbǎi liùshí kuài.",en:"Not expensive — 160 yuan."},{name:"我",zh:"啊？太贵了！",py:"Á? Tài guì le!",en:"What? That's too expensive!"},{name:"老板",zh:"你说多少钱？",py:"Nǐ shuō duōshao qián?",en:"Then how much do you want to pay?"},{name:"我",zh:"一百块。",py:"yìbǎi kuài.",en:"100 yuan."},{name:"老板",zh:"啊？太少了，不卖。",py:"Á? Tài shǎo le, bú mài.",en:"What? That's too little. I won't sell it."},{name:"我",zh:"那我走了。",py:"Nà wǒ zǒu le.",en:"Then I'm leaving."},{name:"老板",zh:"哎，等等，一百五十块怎么样？",py:"Ài, děngdeng, yìbǎi wǔshí kuài zěnmeyàng?",en:"Hey, wait, wait! How about 150 yuan?"},{name:"我",zh:"不要。",py:"Bú yào.",en:"No thanks."},{name:"老板",zh:"不要走。一百四十，一百三十！",py:"Búyào zǒu. Yìbǎi sìshí, yìbǎi sānshí!",en:"Don't go! 140... 130!"},{name:"我",zh:"一百三十太贵了，我是学生，没有钱。",py:"yìbǎi sānshí tài guì le, wǒ shì xuésheng, méiyǒu qián.",en:"130 is too expensive. I'm a student. I don't have any money."},{name:"老板",zh:"最多多少钱？",py:"Zuì duō duōshao qián?",en:"So what's the most you'll pay?"},{name:"我",zh:"一百块。",py:"yìbǎi kuài.",en:"100 yuan."},{name:"老板",zh:"OK了，都退一步，一百二十块怎么样？",py:"OK le, dōu tuì yí bù, yìbǎi èrshí kuài zěnmeyàng?",en:"OK, let's both meet halfway. How about 120 yuan?"},{name:"我",zh:"好吧。",py:"Hǎo ba.",en:"All right."},{name:"老板",zh:"给你衣服。欢迎下次再来！",py:"Gěi nǐ yīfu. Huānyíng xià cì zài lái!",en:"Here you go. Come again next time!"}],vocab:[{w:"发现",py:"fāxiàn",pos:"v.",en:"find"},{w:"砍价",py:"kǎnjià",pos:"v.",en:"bargain"},{w:"便宜",py:"piányi",pos:"adj.",en:"cheap"},{w:"贵",py:"guì",pos:"adj.",en:"expensive"},{w:"对话",py:"duìhuà",pos:"n.",en:"dialogue"},{w:"等等",py:"děngdeng",pos:"",en:"wait a minute"},{w:"退一步",py:"tuì yí bù",pos:"",en:"to make a compromise"},{w:"退",py:"tuì",pos:"v.",en:"retreat"},{w:"步",py:"bù",pos:"n.",en:"step"}],points:[{name:"太＋形容词／动词",en:"too",eg:"太贵了！",egEn:"Too expensive!",zh:"“太＋形容词／动词”中，“太”是副词。表示程度高。句末常带“了”。",enx:"In the structure “太+adj./v.”, “太” is an adverb that indicates “intensity”, and is often used with “了” at the end of the sentence.",egs:["（1）最近我太忙，没时间去你那儿了。","（2）穷和尚太穷了，他只有一个碗和一个杯子。"]},{name:"试试（动词重叠）",en:"have a try",eg:"这件衣服很漂亮，试试吧！",egEn:"This dress is beautiful. Try it on!",zh:"“试”，动词。表示为了看到效果而做某事，尝试。“试试”，两个动词重叠，表示动作持续时间短，可以单独用或在后面加上“试”的对象。口语中还可以说“试一试”、“试一下”。",enx:"“试” is a verb that means “to put to test or trial”. “试试” is a phrase with the structure of verb reduplication and indicates “short duration of an action”. It can be used alone or with an object after it. In oral Chinese, we can also say “试一试” or “试一下”.",egs:["（1）小姐，我能试试这双鞋吗？","（2）我刚买了一个手机，你试试吧。"]}],think:["在你的国家，买东西可以砍价吗？","你在中国买东西砍价吗？","你喜欢砍价吗？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"“我”觉得在中国买东西很特别，是因为（　）。",options:["东西都很便宜","可以砍价","东西都很漂亮","老板都很热情"],answer:1},{q:"砍价有（　）步。",options:["三","四","六","五"],answer:3},{q:"最后“我”用（　）钱买到了那件衣服。",options:["一百块","一百三十块","一百二十块","一百六十块"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"在哪些地方可以砍价？",titleEn:"Where to Bargain in China?",zh:"中国人买东西有砍价的习惯，但不是所有地方都可以砍价。一般来说，大街上的小货摊可以砍价，但是价钱不会便宜很多。不过，在一些小商品市场里，往往可以用要价的 50% 甚至更低的价钱买到商品。但在大型购物中心，如果没有打折降价的标志，一般都明码标价。在这种商场中，如果像文章中那样砍价，会被认为不礼貌，或并不是真心想买东西。",en:"The Chinese like to bargain when shopping, but prices cannot be haggled in all places. Generally speaking, you can bargain at stalls in the street by a small margin. In some small markets, you can pay half the price offered or even lower. In big shopping malls, however, prices are clearly marked and only some have discount labels. In such a shopping centre, it is generally considered impolite or insincere to slash prices in the way mentioned in the text."}},{n:6,title:"自行车王国",py:"Zìxíngchē wángguó",en:"Bicycle Kingdom",chars:193,daodu:"在中国，骑自行车的人特别多，所以中国是个“自行车王国”。",daoduEn:'In China, a huge number of people ride bicycles, so China is called a "Bicycle Kingdom".',paras:[{zh:"因为骑自行车的人非常多，所以有人说中国是“自行车王国”。",py:"Yīnwèi qí zìxíngchē de rén fēicháng duō, suǒyǐ yǒu rén shuō Zhōngguó shì “zìxíngchē wángguó”.",en:'Because so many people ride bicycles, some people say China is a "Bicycle Kingdom".'},{zh:"在中国的城市里，如果是上下班时间，大街上的自行车就像潮水一样。买一辆自行车只要几百元，很便宜，因此很多中国家庭每人都有一辆自行车。中国的一些大学校园很大，很多大学生也有自行车。",py:"Zài Zhōngguó de chéngshì li, rúguǒ shì shàng-xiàbān shíjiān, dàjiē shang de zìxíngchē jiù xiàng cháoshuǐ yíyàng. Mǎi yí liàng zìxíngchē zhǐ yào jǐ bǎi yuán, hěn piányi, yīncǐ hěn duō Zhōngguó jiātíng měi rén dōu yǒu yí liàng zìxíngchē. Zhōngguó de yìxiē dàxué xiàoyuán hěn dà, hěn duō dàxuéshēng yě yǒu zìxíngchē.",en:"In Chinese cities at rush hour, the bicycles on the streets flow like a tide. A bike costs only a few hundred yuan, which is very cheap, so in many Chinese families every person has one. Some Chinese university campuses are very large, so many college students have bikes too."},{zh:"在美国和欧洲，人们骑自行车常常是为了锻炼身体。而在中国，自行车主要是交通工具。自行车非常环保，有很多优点。可是，近年来，中国的小汽车越来越多，大城市的堵车也越来越严重。真希望中国继续做一个“自行车王国”。",py:"Zài Měiguó hé Ōuzhōu, rénmen qí zìxíngchē chángcháng shì wèile duànliàn shēntǐ. Ér zài Zhōngguó, zìxíngchē zhǔyào shì jiāotōng gōngjù. Zìxíngchē fēicháng huánbǎo, yǒu hěn duō yōudiǎn. Kěshì, jìnniánlái, Zhōngguó de xiǎoqìchē yuèláiyuè duō, dà chéngshì de dǔchē yě yuèláiyuè yánzhòng. Zhēn xīwàng Zhōngguó jìxù zuò yí gè “zìxíngchē wángguó”.",en:'In America and Europe, people often ride bikes to get exercise. But in China, the bicycle is mainly a way of getting around. Bikes are very green and have many advantages. However, in recent years there have been more and more cars in China, and traffic jams in big cities are getting worse and worse. I really hope China will stay a "Bicycle Kingdom".'}],vocab:[{w:"骑",py:"qí",pos:"v.",en:"ride"},{w:"大街",py:"dàjiē",pos:"n.",en:"avenue"},{w:"潮水",py:"cháoshuǐ",pos:"n.",en:"tide"},{w:"锻炼",py:"duànliàn",pos:"v.",en:"exercise"},{w:"交通",py:"jiāotōng",pos:"n.",en:"transportation"},{w:"工具",py:"gōngjù",pos:"n.",en:"vehicle"},{w:"环保",py:"huánbǎo",pos:"n.",en:"environmental protection"},{w:"优点",py:"yōudiǎn",pos:"n.",en:"merit"},{w:"堵车",py:"dǔchē",pos:"v.",en:"be traffic-jammed"},{w:"严重",py:"yánzhòng",pos:"adj.",en:"severe"},{w:"继续",py:"jìxù",pos:"v.",en:"continue"}],points:[{name:"因此",en:"therefore, so",eg:"自行车很便宜，因此很多中国家庭每人都有一辆自行车。",egEn:"Bikes are cheap in China, so that in many Chinese families, everyone has a bike.",zh:"在“A，因此B”中，A引出原因，“因此B”说明结果。",enx:"In “A，因此B”, A indicates “reasons”, while “因此B” introduces results.",egs:["（1）我喜欢中国，因此来北京学习汉语。","（2）我昨天睡得太晚了，因此今天上课迟到了。"]},{name:"越来越",en:"more and more",eg:"近年来，中国的小汽车越来越多，大城市的堵车也越来越严重。",egEn:"In recent years, there are more and more cars in China. As a result, traffic jams in big cities are getting worse and worse.",zh:"“越来越”表示程度随时间的推移而变化。只能有一个主语。",enx:"“越来越” means “a rise in degree as time goes on”. There is only one subject in this structure.",egs:["（1）到了五月，南京的天气就越来越热了。","（2）事情越来越有希望，咱们再等一等吧。"]}],think:["欧洲人骑自行车主要是为了什么？","你觉得自行车有什么优点？","“我”为什么希望中国继续做一个“自行车王国”？"],tf:[{q:"中国是“自行车王国”，因为中国的自行车最好。",a:!1},{q:"在中国，现在买一辆自行车不会花很多钱。",a:!0},{q:"欧洲人、美国人骑自行车的原因和中国人不一样。",a:!0},{q:"“我”觉得中国应该有更多的小汽车。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"自行车在中国",titleEn:"Bicycles in China",zh:"以前，自行车在中国的家庭中曾经占据重要地位。它与手表、缝纫机，被称为“三大件”，是中国家庭财富的象征。改革开放（1978年）以后，人们的生活水平提高了，特别是近些年，私家车已经在某种程度上取代了自行车，成为许多城市居民的代步工具。但越来越多的机动车给交通和环境带来了不良影响，因此，自行车在一定时期内仍将是政府提倡和人们喜爱的交通工具。",en:"Bicycles played an important role in the Chinese families before. They were one of the “Three Big Wares” together with watches and sewing machines, which were regarded as a symbol of family wealth. After the implementation of the policy of reform and opening up since 1978, living standard has improved in China. In recent years in particular, cars have been gradually taking the place of bicycles and are becoming the main transportation means of townsfolks. But more and more automobiles have caused traffic and environmental problems. Thus, bicycles will still be promoted by the government and remain popular among the Chinese people."}},{n:7,title:"看风景还是拍照片？",py:"Kàn fēngjǐng háishi pāi zhàopiàn?",en:"Sight-seeing or Photographing?",chars:265,daodu:"旅行的时候，有的人喜欢看风景（fēngjǐng: scenery），有的人喜欢拍照片。你在旅行的时候喜欢拍照片吗？",daoduEn:"When traveling, some people like to look at the scenery, and some like to take photos. Do you like taking photos when you travel?",paras:[{zh:"你知道中国人旅行有什么特点吗？",py:"Nǐ zhīdào Zhōngguórén lǚxíng yǒu shénme tèdiǎn ma?",en:"Do you know what's special about the way Chinese people travel?"},{zh:"有一张很有趣的画，告诉大家中国人和西方人在旅游时的表现是不同的。右边的画里有一只眼睛，代表西方人，意思是西方人旅游的时候，喜欢用自己的眼睛欣赏美景。左边的画里是一架相机，代表中国人，意思是中国人旅游的时候，喜欢带着相机到处拍照。有人说他们是“上车睡觉，下车拍照，一问什么都不知道”。",py:"Yǒu yì zhāng hěn yǒuqù de huà, gàosu dàjiā Zhōngguórén hé Xīfāngrén zài lǚyóu shí de biǎoxiàn shì bùtóng de. Yòubian de huà li yǒu yì zhī yǎnjing, dàibiǎo Xīfāngrén, yìsi shì Xīfāngrén lǚyóu de shíhou, xǐhuan yòng zìjǐ de yǎnjing xīnshǎng měijǐng. Zuǒbian de huà li shì yí jià xiàngjī, dàibiǎo Zhōngguórén, yìsi shì Zhōngguórén lǚyóu de shíhou, xǐhuan dàizhe xiàngjī dàochù pāizhào. Yǒu rén shuō tāmen shì “shàng chē shuìjiào, xià chē pāizhào, yí wèn shénme dōu bù zhīdào”.",en:`There's a funny picture that shows how differently Chinese and Western people behave when they travel. The picture on the right has an eye in it. It stands for Western people: when they travel, they like to enjoy the beautiful scenery with their own eyes. The picture on the left has a camera in it. It stands for Chinese people: when they travel, they like to carry a camera and take photos everywhere. Some people describe them like this: "Get on the bus — sleep; get off the bus — snap photos; ask them anything — they know nothing."`},{zh:"确实，以前中国人旅游的机会很少，出国旅游的机会更少，所以，很多人都喜欢用相机代替眼睛。他们不停地拍照，回到家以后，一边看照片，一边回忆去过的地方。随着中国经济的发展，越来越多的中国人出去旅游，人们也将越来越意识到，看着照片回忆虽然重要，但更重要的还是用自己的眼睛欣赏眼前的美景。",py:"Quèshí, yǐqián Zhōngguórén lǚyóu de jīhuì hěn shǎo, chūguó lǚyóu de jīhuì gèng shǎo, suǒyǐ, hěn duō rén dōu xǐhuan yòng xiàngjī dàitì yǎnjing. Tāmen bùtíng de pāizhào, huídào jiā yǐhòu, yìbiān kàn zhàopiàn, yìbiān huíyì qùguo de dìfang. Suízhe Zhōngguó jīngjì de fāzhǎn, yuèláiyuè duō de Zhōngguórén chūqù lǚyóu, rénmen yě jiāng yuèláiyuè yìshí dào, kànzhe zhàopiàn huíyì suīrán zhòngyào, dàn gèng zhòngyào de háishi yòng zìjǐ de yǎnjing xīnshǎng yǎnqián de měijǐng.",en:"It's true that in the past, Chinese people had few chances to travel, and even fewer chances to go abroad, so many people liked to use their cameras in place of their eyes. They took photos nonstop, and back home they would look at the photos and remember the places they had been. As China's economy grows, more and more Chinese people are traveling, and they will come to realize that, although remembering a trip through photos matters, what matters more is enjoying the beautiful view in front of you with your own eyes."}],vocab:[{w:"特点",py:"tèdiǎn",pos:"n.",en:"trait"},{w:"欣赏",py:"xīnshǎng",pos:"v.",en:"appreciate"},{w:"架",py:"jià",pos:"m.",en:"(used for sth. with a stand or mechanism)"},{w:"拍照",py:"pāizhào",pos:"v.",en:"take photos"},{w:"确实",py:"quèshí",pos:"adv.",en:"indeed"},{w:"机会",py:"jīhuì",pos:"n.",en:"chance"},{w:"意识",py:"yìshí",pos:"v.",en:"realize"}],points:[{name:"代表",en:"represent, stand for",eg:"右边的画里有一只眼睛，代表西方人。",egEn:"There is an eye in the right picture, standing for the Westerners.",zh:"“代表”，动词。表示用人或事物表示某种特定的意义或概念。“代表”前面的内容是客观的、可以被感知的事物，后面的内容通常是这种事物被赋予的某种意义。",enx:"“代表” is a verb that means “certain people or things can serve as a sign or symbol (of somebody or something)”. The part before “代表” is usually an objective thing that can be perceived, while the part after “代表” is the meaning represented by the previous part.",egs:["（1）中国人喜欢数字“8”，因为“8”代表“发”（有很多钱）。","（2）在有的国家，点头代表不同意，摇头代表同意。"]},{name:"A 代替 B",en:"substitute",eg:"很多人都喜欢用相机代替眼睛。",egEn:"There are many people who like to use their cameras instead of their eyes.",zh:"“A 代替 B”中，“代替”是动词。这一句式表示用 A 换 B，由 A 起 B 的作用。",enx:"“代替” in “A代替B” is a verb. This pattern means “to substitute B with A”, “A plays the role of B”.",egs:["（1）今天王老师生病了，张老师代替他给我们上课。","（2）比赛就要开始了，小明还没来，我们找谁来代替他呢？"]},{name:"随着",en:"happen along with",eg:"随着中国经济的发展，越来越多的中国人出去旅游。",egEn:"With the economic development of China, more and more people are beginning to travel.",zh:"“随着”，动词。是“跟着”的意思。",enx:"“随着” is a verb that means something happens along with something else.",egs:["（1）随着我的汉语水平的提高，我越来越喜欢北京的生活了。","（2）随着春天的到来，公园里更加热闹了。"]}],think:["你觉得旅行时相机很重要吗？为什么？","西方人和中国人的旅行方式，你喜欢哪一种？为什么？"],tf:[{q:"以前中国人旅游的机会不多。",a:!0},{q:"中国人出去旅游很喜欢拍照。",a:!0},{q:"西方人旅游更喜欢用眼睛去欣赏美景。",a:!0},{q:"越来越多的中国人将出去旅行，因为他们有钱了。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"旅游——中国人的新时尚",titleEn:"Travelling—the Latest Fashion of the Chinese",zh:"随着人们收入的提高，旅游已日渐成为中国人的时尚生活方式。中国旅游资源丰富，传统的旅游地区有北京、西安等历史名城。近年来，新疆、西藏、云南等西部少数民族聚居区也受到越来越多国内外旅行者的青睐。同时，出国游不再是奢侈行为，很多人把东南亚、欧洲等地区作为出行的目的地。",en:"As people's incomes increase, travelling is becoming a popular life style of the Chinese. China is rich in travelling resources. Traditional places of interests include some historical cities like Beijing and Xi'an. However, in recent years, residential areas of ethnic groups in the western areas of China, like Xinjiang, Tibet and Yunnan, are favored by more and more travellers from home and abroad. Travelling abroad is no longer a luxury. Many people choose regions like Southeast Asia and Europe as their travelling destinations."}},{n:8,title:"喝醉了",py:"Hēzuì le",en:"Drunk Talk",chars:178,daodu:`你爱喝酒吗？
喝酒以后闹过笑话吗？`,daoduEn:"Do you like drinking? Have you ever made a fool of yourself after drinking?",paras:[{zh:"有父子两人，都是酒鬼，他们特别爱喝酒，也经常喝醉。",py:"Yǒu fù-zǐ liǎng rén, dōu shì jiǔguǐ, tāmen tèbié ài hējiǔ, yě jīngcháng hēzuì.",en:"There were a father and son who were both drunkards. They loved drinking and were often drunk."},{zh:"一天，父亲在外面喝得大醉，摇摇晃晃回到他们住的公寓。他们家住在三楼，可是他在二楼就敲门了。二楼的人没开门就说：“你们家在楼上！”父亲好不容易回到家，进门后，他盯着儿子的脸看了一会儿，生气地说：“奇怪，你的脸怎么变成三个了？你这样一个奇怪的东西，我的房子一定不留给你！”他的儿子也在家喝得大醉，听了爸爸的话，不服气地说：“那更好！像这样摇摇晃晃的房子，给我，我还不要呢！”",py:"Yì tiān, fùqin zài wàimiàn hē de dà zuì, yáoyáohuànghuàng huídào tāmen zhù de gōngyù. Tāmen jiā zhù zài sān lóu, kěshì tā zài èr lóu jiù qiāo mén le. Èr lóu de rén méi kāi mén jiù shuō: “Nǐmen jiā zài lóu shàng!” Fùqin hǎobù róngyì huídào jiā, jìnmén hòu, tā dīngzhe érzi de liǎn kànle yíhuìr, shēngqì de shuō: “Qíguài, nǐ de liǎn zěnme biànchéng sān gè le? Nǐ zhèyàng yí gè qíguài de dōngxi, wǒ de fángzi yídìng bù liúgěi nǐ!” Tā de érzi yě zài jiā hē de dà zuì, tīngle bàba de huà, bù fúqì de shuō: “Nà gèng hǎo! Xiàng zhèyàng yáoyáohuànghuàng de fángzi, gěi wǒ, wǒ hái bú yào ne!”",en:`One day, the father got very drunk while he was out and staggered back to the apartment building where they lived. Their home was on the third floor, but he knocked on a door on the second floor. Without even opening the door, the people on the second floor said, "Your place is upstairs!" When the father finally made it home, he stared at his son's face for a while and said angrily, "Strange — why do you have three faces? A weird thing like you — I'm certainly not leaving my house to you!" The son, who had also gotten very drunk at home, heard this and shot back, "Fine by me! A house that sways back and forth like this — even if you gave it to me, I wouldn't want it!"`}],vocab:[{w:"酒鬼",py:"jiǔguǐ",pos:"n.",en:"drunkard"},{w:"外面",py:"wàimiàn",pos:"n.",en:"outside"},{w:"公寓",py:"gōngyù",pos:"n.",en:"apartment"},{w:"敲",py:"qiāo",pos:"v.",en:"knock"},{w:"盯",py:"dīng",pos:"v.",en:"stare at"},{w:"生气",py:"shēngqì",pos:"v.",en:"get angry"},{w:"留",py:"liú",pos:"v.",en:"leave"},{w:"服气",py:"fúqì",pos:"v.",en:"be convinced"}],points:[{name:"喝得大醉",en:"very drunk",eg:"一天，父亲在外面喝得大醉。",egEn:"One day, the father got drunk outside.",zh:"“喝得大醉”是“动词＋得＋形容词”的结构，其中形容词作动词的补语，表示动作或动作发出者的状态。",enx:"The structure of “喝得大醉” is “v.＋得＋adj.”. The adjective is used as a complement of the verb and indicates “the state of the action or the person who does the action”.",egs:["（1）她中国菜做得非常好。","（2）他的汉语说得真棒！"]},{name:"摇摇晃晃",en:"stumble",eg:"父亲摇摇晃晃回到他们住的公寓。",egEn:"The father stumbled back to the apartment where they lived.",zh:"“摇摇晃晃”，是动词“摇晃”的AABB式重叠形式，表示摇摆晃动的样子。",enx:"“摇摇晃晃” is a reduplication pattern of AABB of the verb “摇晃” and indicates “the state of stumbling”.",egs:["（1）这个人不喜欢工作，每天吃吃喝喝，什么也不做。","（2）生日晚会的时候，大家在一起说说笑笑，很热闹。"]}],think:["父亲为什么摇摇晃晃地回家？","儿子觉得父亲的房子好不好？为什么？"],tf:[{q:"父亲的房子不好，摇摇晃晃的。",a:!1},{q:"儿子也喜欢喝酒。",a:!0},{q:"儿子很奇怪，有时候有三张脸。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"父亲和儿子都喜欢（　）。",options:["吸烟","唱歌","喝茶","喝酒"],answer:3},{q:"他们家住在（　）。",options:["一楼","二楼","三楼","四楼"],answer:2},{q:"因为（　），所以二楼的人没有开门。",options:["父亲敲错了门","二楼没有人","二楼的人在睡觉","二楼的人不认识父亲"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"中国的“酒文化”",titleEn:"Chinese “Wine Culture”",zh:"酒在中国有着独特的地位，流淌在整个中华民族五千年的文明史中，影响着中国人生活的很多方面。从文学、饮食、保健到人际交往，从国宴到普通人的聚餐，到处都能看到酒的身影。古诗中也有无数关于酒的名句。因为，中国古代文人诗必饮酒，酒必赋诗。像上图中的陶渊明和左图中的李白都在酒后留下了许多伟大的诗篇。",en:"Wine plays a unique role in China, steeped in the Chinese civilization for five thousand years. It has influenced many aspects of the Chinese people’s life, like culture, diet, health care and social communication. It can be seen in state banquets and ordinary gatherings of common people. There are also numerous famous lines about wine in classic Chinese poems. In ancient times, Chinese men of letters always drank when they wrote poetry, just as shown in the pictures of Tao Yuanming (above) and Li Bai (left), two great poets who created many masterpieces after their drinks."}},{n:9,title:"磨斧子",py:"Mó fǔzi",en:"Whet the Axe",chars:201,daodu:"在人的一生（yīshēng: all one's life）中，我们应该经常停下来想一想，这样才能走得更快、更好。",daoduEn:"In life, we should often stop and think. Only then can we go faster and do better.",paras:[{zh:"有个年轻的伐木工人，好不容易找到了一份工作，工作条件很好，钱也不少。老板还给了他一把好斧子。他很喜欢这份工作，下决心好好干。",py:"Yǒu gè niánqīng de fámù gōngrén, hǎobù róngyì zhǎodàole yí fèn gōngzuò, gōngzuò tiáojiàn hěn hǎo, qián yě bù shǎo. Lǎobǎn hái gěile tā yì bǎ hǎo fǔzi. Tā hěn xǐhuan zhè fèn gōngzuò, xià juéxīn hǎohǎo gàn.",en:"A young lumberjack finally found a job after a lot of trouble. The working conditions were good and the pay was good too. The boss even gave him a good axe. He liked the job very much and made up his mind to work hard."},{zh:"第一天，他砍了十八棵树。老板很高兴地鼓励他：“不错！”年轻的工人很高兴。",py:"Dì-yī tiān, tā kǎnle shíbā kē shù. Lǎobǎn hěn gāoxìng de gǔlì tā: “Bú cuò!” Niánqīng de gōngrén hěn gāoxìng.",en:'On the first day, he cut down eighteen trees. The boss was very pleased and encouraged him: "Well done!" The young worker was very happy.'},{zh:"第二天，他一直工作，但是只砍了十五棵树。",py:"Dì-èr tiān, tā yìzhí gōngzuò, dànshì zhǐ kǎnle shíwǔ kē shù.",en:"On the second day, he worked nonstop, but cut down only fifteen trees."},{zh:"第三天，他还是非常非常努力，可是只砍了十棵树。",py:"Dì-sān tiān, tā háishi fēicháng fēicháng nǔlì, kěshì zhǐ kǎnle shí kē shù.",en:"On the third day, he still worked very, very hard, but cut down only ten trees."},{zh:"工人感到很惭愧，到老板那里道歉说：“不知道为什么，我已经很努力了，但是我的力气却越来越小。”",py:"Gōngrén gǎndào hěn cánkuì, dào lǎobǎn nàli dàoqiàn shuō: “Bù zhīdào wèishénme, wǒ yǐjīng hěn nǔlì le, dànshì wǒ de lìqi què yuèláiyuè xiǎo.”",en:`The worker felt ashamed. He went to the boss and apologized: "I don't know why. I've been working very hard, but I'm getting weaker and weaker."`},{zh:"老板问他：“你上一次磨斧子是在什么时候？”",py:"Lǎobǎn wèn tā: “Nǐ shàng yí cì mó fǔzi shì zài shénme shíhou?”",en:'The boss asked him, "When was the last time you sharpened your axe?"'},{zh:"“磨斧子？”工人突然明白了，“我天天忙着砍树，但忘了磨斧子了！”",py:"“Mó fǔzi?” Gōngrén tūrán míngbai le, “Wǒ tiāntiān mángzhe kǎn shù, dàn wàngle mó fǔzi le!”",en:`"Sharpen my axe?" Suddenly the worker understood. "I've been so busy cutting trees every day that I forgot to sharpen my axe!"`}],vocab:[{w:"伐木",py:"fámù",pos:"v.",en:"lumber"},{w:"条件",py:"tiáojiàn",pos:"n.",en:"condition"},{w:"斧子",py:"fǔzi",pos:"n.",en:"axe"},{w:"砍",py:"kǎn",pos:"v.",en:"cut down"},{w:"惭愧",py:"cánkuì",pos:"adj.",en:"ashamed"},{w:"道歉",py:"dàoqiàn",pos:"v.",en:"apologize"},{w:"力气",py:"lìqi",pos:"n.",en:"strength"},{w:"磨",py:"mó",pos:"v.",en:"sharpen"},{w:"明白",py:"míngbai",pos:"v.",en:"understand, realize"},{w:"忙",py:"máng",pos:"v.",en:"be busy"}],points:[{name:"下决心",en:"make up one's mind",eg:"他很喜欢这份工作，下决心好好干。",egEn:"He liked his job very much, and was determined to do it well.",zh:"“下决心”，表示拿定主意，有决心干某事。“决心”，名词。表示坚定的意志。",enx:"“下决心” indicates “to form a determination to do something”. “决心” is a noun that means “strong will”.",egs:["（1）我常常因为声调闹笑话，所以我下决心学好汉语的发音。","（2）北京的房子很贵，所以许多人下决心不买房子了。"]},{name:"鼓励",en:"inspire, encourage",eg:"老板很高兴地鼓励他：“不错！”",egEn:"The boss was very happy and commended, “Well done!”",zh:"“鼓励”，动词。是“激发、勉励”的意思。",enx:"“鼓励” is a verb that means “to inspire and encourage”.",egs:["（1）老师常常鼓励我们，我们的学习也更努力了。","（2）非常感谢你对我的鼓励，我一定好好干！"]}],think:["为什么这个工人砍的树越来越少？","这个故事告诉我们什么？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"伐木工人很喜欢这份工作，不是因为（　）。",options:["工作条件很好","钱不少","工作很轻松","老板给了他一把好斧子"],answer:2},{q:"从第一天到第三天，工人砍的树（　）。",options:["越来越多","越来越少","每天一样多","先少后多"],answer:1},{q:"第三天，工人感到（　）。",options:["很高兴","很轻松","很惭愧","很生气"],answer:2},{q:"老板认为，这个工人砍树越来越少的原因是（　）。",options:["他不够努力","他很久没有磨斧子了","他的力气越来越小","树越来越大"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"磨刀不误砍柴工",titleEn:"Whetting the Axe Will Not Delay the Cutting of Firewood",zh:"中国有句老话，叫“磨刀不误砍柴工”。意思是说，花点时间把斧子磨得锋利些，就可以提高砍柴的效率，不会耽误砍柴的时间。这句话强调花时间做好准备工作，不会耽误工作进度，而且往往能取得“事半功倍”的效果。",en:"There was a Chinese saying, “Whetting the axe will not delay the cutting of firewood”. This saying tells us that spending some time sharpening the axe will enhance efficiency. This proverb implies that good preparation saves time, just as a stitch in time saves nine."}},{n:10,title:"北京的出租车",py:"Běijīng de chūzūchē",en:"Taxis in Beijing",chars:208,daodu:`来过北京的人都说，
北京的出租车司机真热情。`,daoduEn:"Everyone who has been to Beijing says Beijing taxi drivers are really friendly.",paras:[{zh:"在北京乘出租车很方便。起步价是三千米十块钱，之后一千米两块钱。比如，从机场到北京大学四十多千米，大概一百块钱。",py:"Zài Běijīng chéng chūzūchē hěn fāngbiàn. Qǐbùjià shì sān qiānmǐ shí kuài qián, zhīhòu yì qiānmǐ liǎng kuài qián. Bǐrú, cóng jīchǎng dào Běijīng Dàxué sìshí duō qiānmǐ, dàgài yìbǎi kuài qián.",en:"Taking a taxi in Beijing is very convenient. The starting fare is 10 yuan for the first 3 kilometers, and after that it's 2 yuan per kilometer. For example, it's a little over 40 kilometers from the airport to Peking University, which costs about 100 yuan."},{zh:"北京人一般把出租车叫做“的士”或者“出租”，坐出租车叫“打的”、“打车”。北京的出租车司机被亲切地称为“的哥”、“的姐”。但“的哥”、“的姐”很少当面用，当面一般说“师傅”。北京的出租车司机很有意思，他们喜欢和你聊天儿，而且他们知道很多事情，你有什么不知道的，都可以问他们。他们非常热情，愿意回答各种各样的问题。",py:"Běijīngrén yìbān bǎ chūzūchē jiàozuò “dīshì” huòzhě “chūzū”, zuò chūzūchē jiào “dǎdī”, “dǎchē”. Běijīng de chūzūchē sījī bèi qīnqiè de chēngwéi “dīgē”, “dījiě”. Dàn “dīgē”, “dījiě” hěn shǎo dāngmiàn yòng, dāngmiàn yìbān shuō “shīfu”. Běijīng de chūzūchē sījī hěn yǒu yìsi, tāmen xǐhuan hé nǐ liáotiānr, érqiě tāmen zhīdào hěn duō shìqing, nǐ yǒu shénme bù zhīdào de, dōu kěyǐ wèn tāmen. Tāmen fēicháng rèqíng, yuànyì huídá gèzhǒng-gèyàng de wèntí.",en:`Beijing people usually call a taxi a "dīshì" (from the Cantonese word for "taxi") or a "chūzū", and taking a taxi is called "dǎdī" or "dǎchē". Beijing taxi drivers are affectionately called "dīgē" (taxi brother) and "dījiě" (taxi sister). But people rarely use these names to a driver's face; face to face they usually say "shīfu" (master). Beijing taxi drivers are a lot of fun. They like chatting with you, and they know a lot, so you can ask them anything you don't know. They're very warm and happy to answer all kinds of questions.`},{zh:"另外，大家在北京坐出租车的时候要记住：第一，别忘了你的东西；第二，从右边车门上下车。",py:"Lìngwài, dàjiā zài Běijīng zuò chūzūchē de shíhou yào jìzhù: dì-yī, bié wàngle nǐ de dōngxi; dì-èr, cóng yòubian chēmén shàng-xiàchē.",en:"One more thing: when you take a taxi in Beijing, remember two things. First, don't leave your things behind. Second, get in and out by the door on the right side."}],vocab:[{w:"起步价",py:"qǐbùjià",pos:"n.",en:"starting price"},{w:"之后",py:"zhīhòu",pos:"n.",en:"from then on"},{w:"大概",py:"dàgài",pos:"adv.",en:"approximately"},{w:"亲切",py:"qīnqiè",pos:"adj.",en:"affectionate"},{w:"当面",py:"dāngmiàn",pos:"adv.",en:"face to face"},{w:"愿意",py:"yuànyì",pos:"v.",en:"be willing"},{w:"各种各样",py:"gèzhǒng-gèyàng",pos:"",en:"all kinds of"},{w:"另外",py:"lìngwài",pos:"conj.",en:"in addition"}],points:[{name:"从……到……",en:"from ... to ...",eg:"从机场到北京大学四十多千米，大概一百块钱。",egEn:"It is more than 40 kilometers from the airport to Peking University and costs about 100 yuan.",zh:"“从……到……”，由一个点到另一个点，表示范围、距离、状态或时间的变化。",enx:"“从……到……” means “from ... to ...”, and is used to show changes of scope, distance, condition and time.",egs:["（1）从北京到东京，坐飞机大概要三个小时。","（2）我每天从早上八点到中午十二点有课。"]},{name:"别",en:"not to do",eg:"别忘了你的东西。",egEn:"Do not leave your belongings behind.",zh:"“别”，副词。表示阻止或劝阻，后面一般加阻止或劝阻的行为动作。",enx:"“别” is an adverb that means “to advise somebody not to do something”. “别” is usually used before a verb that indicates “the action to be avoided”.",egs:["（1）现在都八点半了，以后早点儿来，别迟到。","（2）下雨了，今天别出去了。"]}],think:["你觉得在北京坐出租车贵吗？","北京人一般把出租车叫什么？","你觉得北京的出租车司机怎么样？"],tf:[{q:"北京出租车起步价是十千米三块钱。",a:!1},{q:"出租车三千米以后每千米两块钱。",a:!0},{q:"北京的出租车司机喜欢和客人聊天儿。",a:!0},{q:"你可以问出租车司机各种问题。",a:!0},{q:"“我”认为北京的出租车司机很热情。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"黄包车的今昔",titleEn:"Rickshaw's Today and Yesterday",zh:"黄包车是一种用人力拖拉的双轮客运工具，1874 年从日本输入上海，后来在中国各大城市纷纷使用，一直到 20 世纪 50 年代被送进博物馆，黄包车才一度退出了历史舞台。但近年来，在北京的“胡同游”、杭州的“西湖游”等旅游活动中，黄包车又恢复了往日的生机。",en:"A rickshaw is a small two-wheeled manually-pulled passenger vehicle. It was introduced into Shanghai from Japan in 1874. From then on, it was widely used in big cities in China until the 1950s when it was sent to museums and became part of the history. However, in recent years, it has revived as a tourist attraction like Beijing's “Hutong Tour” and Hangzhou's “West Lake Sightseeing Tour”."}},{n:11,title:"中国人越来越“贵”？",py:"Zhōngguórén yuèláiyuè “guì”?",en:"Rich or Expensive?",chars:220,daodu:"在学习汉语的时候，每个人也许都闹过笑话。你呢？",daoduEn:"Everyone probably makes funny mistakes when learning Chinese. What about you?",paras:[{zh:"外国留学生学汉语，常常闹笑话。",py:"Wàiguó liúxuéshēng xué Hànyǔ, chángcháng nào xiàohua.",en:"Foreign students learning Chinese often make funny mistakes."},{zh:"第一个学生不知道“富”和“贵”的不同，造句说：“现在中国人越来越贵了。”他不知道只有东西才说“贵”。我们可以说中国的东西不贵，很便宜。",py:"Dì-yī gè xuéshēng bù zhīdào “fù” hé “guì” de bùtóng, zàojù shuō: “Xiànzài Zhōngguórén yuèláiyuè guì le.” Tā bù zhīdào zhǐyǒu dōngxi cái shuō “guì”. Wǒmen kěyǐ shuō Zhōngguó de dōngxi bú guì, hěn piányi.",en:`The first student didn't know the difference between "fù" (富, rich) and "guì" (贵, expensive). He made this sentence: "Chinese people are getting more and more expensive." He didn't know that "guì" is only used for things. We can say that things in China aren't expensive — they're cheap.`},{zh:"第二个女生的作业里有这样的句子：“我每天都很忙，白天上课，晚上练习生子（字）。”“生字”是不认识的字，“生子”是生孩子。太不一样了！",py:"Dì-èr gè nǚshēng de zuòyè li yǒu zhèyàng de jùzi: “Wǒ měi tiān dōu hěn máng, báitiān shàngkè, wǎnshang liànxí shēng zǐ (zì).” “Shēngzì” shì bú rènshi de zì, “shēngzǐ” shì shēng háizi. Tài bù yíyàng le!",en:`The second student, a girl, wrote this sentence in her homework: "I'm very busy every day. I have classes during the day, and in the evening I practice shēngzǐ (生子)" — she meant shēngzì (生字). "Shēngzì" means new characters you don't know yet, but "shēngzǐ" means having babies. What a difference!`},{zh:"第三个男生在翻译时，把“张太太和她的先生离婚了，我很同情她”翻译成“张太太和她的先生离婚了，我很对不起她”。这个男生不明白“同情”和“对不起”意思完全不同。“我很对不起她”表示张太太和她的先生离婚这件事“我”有责任。而“我很同情她”是对她表示关心。",py:"Dì-sān gè nánshēng zài fānyì shí, bǎ “Zhāng tàitai hé tā de xiānsheng líhūn le, wǒ hěn tóngqíng tā” fānyì chéng “Zhāng tàitai hé tā de xiānsheng líhūn le, wǒ hěn duìbuqǐ tā”. Zhège nánshēng bù míngbai “tóngqíng” hé “duìbuqǐ” yìsi wánquán bù tóng. “Wǒ hěn duìbuqǐ tā” biǎoshì Zhāng tàitai hé tā de xiānsheng líhūn zhè jiàn shì “wǒ” yǒu zérèn. Ér “wǒ hěn tóngqíng tā” shì duì tā biǎoshì guānxīn.",en:`The third student, a boy, was translating, and he turned "Mrs. Zhang divorced her husband, and I feel sorry for her (同情她)" into "Mrs. Zhang divorced her husband, and I owe her an apology (对不起她)." He didn't understand that "tóngqíng" and "duìbuqǐ" mean completely different things. "我很对不起她" means "I" am to blame for Mrs. Zhang's divorce, while "我很同情她" shows that you care about her.`}],vocab:[{w:"造句",py:"zàojù",pos:"v.",en:"make sentences"},{w:"生子",py:"shēngzǐ",pos:"",en:"give birth to a baby"},{w:"太太",py:"tàitai",pos:"n.",en:"Mrs, madame"},{w:"离婚",py:"líhūn",pos:"v.",en:"divorce"},{w:"完全",py:"wánquán",pos:"adv.",en:"completely"},{w:"责任",py:"zérèn",pos:"n.",en:"responsibility"},{w:"关心",py:"guānxīn",pos:"v.",en:"be concerned about"}],points:[{name:"同情",en:"sympathize with",eg:"张太太和她的先生离婚了，我很同情她。",egEn:"Mrs. Zhang and her husband are divorced. I sympathize with her.",zh:"“同情”，动词。是“对别人的不幸遭遇心中产生相同的感情并表示关心”的意思。",enx:"“同情” is a verb that means “to feel sorry for someone because of his/her misfortune and show your concern to him/her”.",egs:["（1）他三岁的时候就没有了父母，我们都很同情他。","（2）奶奶很有同情心，总是帮助有困难的人。"]},{name:"把……翻译成……",en:"translate ... into ...",eg:"第三个男生把“……我很同情她”翻译成“……我很对不起她”。",egEn:"The third boy translated “…… 我很同情她” into “…… 我很对不起她”.",zh:"“把……翻译成……”是“把 + A + 动词 + 成 + B”的结构。这一结构常常表示“把 A 改变成了 B”的意思。",enx:"“把……翻译成……” is an example of the structure “把 + A + v. + 成 + B”. This structure usually means “to change A into B”.",egs:["（1）他把“请问”说成了“亲吻”。","（2）他把“明天上午上课”听成了“明天下午上课”。"]}],think:["“富”和“贵”是什么意思？常常在什么时候用？","你在学习汉语时闹过什么笑话吗？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"第一个学生的意思是，现在的中国人比以前（　）。",options:["忙","有钱","多","快乐"],answer:1},{q:"第二个学生晚上（　）。",options:["上课","生孩子","练习生字","看电视"],answer:2},{q:"这篇文章主要说的是（　）。",options:["中国人越来越有钱","汉字很难写","怎么翻译句子","留学生学汉语时闹的笑话"],answer:3}],tip:{title:"中国传统乐器——二胡",titleEn:"A Traditional Chinese Musical Instrument—Erhu",zh:"二胡是中国传统的乐器。因为乐器上有两条弦，所以得名。二胡最早发源于中国古代北部地区的一个少数民族，至今已有一千多年的历史。二胡的音色具有柔美抒情的特点，发出的声音极富歌唱性，像人的歌声一样。",en:"Erhu is a traditional Chinese musical instrument. Its name comes from its two parallel strings. Erhu originated over one thousand years ago in an ethnic group in the north of ancient China. The timbre of Erhu is soft, beautiful, affective and resembles human singing sound."}},{n:12,title:"黑猩猩戒烟",py:"Hēixīngxing jiè yān",en:"The Chimpanzee Quitted Smoking",chars:219,daodu:"你吸烟吗？有没有戒过烟？成功了吗？下面是一个黑猩猩吸烟、戒烟的有趣故事。",daoduEn:"Do you smoke? Have you ever tried to quit? Did you succeed? Here is a funny story about a chimpanzee who smoked — and then quit.",paras:[{zh:"非非是动物园的一只黑猩猩，它非常可爱。可是，来动物园玩儿的人常常向它扔烟头。慢慢地，非非也开始吸烟。它越吸越多，有时一天要吸十支烟。一年以后，非非变成了一个大烟鬼，没有烟它就不吃东西。",py:"Fēifēi shì dòngwùyuán de yì zhī hēixīngxing, tā fēicháng kě'ài. Kěshì, lái dòngwùyuán wánr de rén chángcháng xiàng tā rēng yāntóu. Mànmàn de, Fēifēi yě kāishǐ xīyān. Tā yuè xī yuè duō, yǒushí yì tiān yào xī shí zhī yān. Yì nián yǐhòu, Fēifēi biànchéngle yí gè dà yānguǐ, méiyǒu yān tā jiù bù chī dōngxi.",en:"Feifei was a chimpanzee at the zoo, and it was very cute. But visitors to the zoo often threw cigarette butts at it. Little by little, Feifei started smoking too. It smoked more and more — sometimes as many as ten cigarettes a day. A year later, Feifei had become a heavy smoker. Without cigarettes, it wouldn't eat."},{zh:"因为吸烟太多，非非的身体越来越差。在春天，非非感冒了好几次，而且还得了肺炎。",py:"Yīnwèi xīyān tài duō, Fēifēi de shēntǐ yuèláiyuè chà. Zài chūntiān, Fēifēi gǎnmàole hǎo jǐ cì, érqiě hái déle fèiyán.",en:"Because it smoked too much, Feifei's health got worse and worse. In the spring, Feifei caught a cold several times and even got pneumonia."},{zh:"动物园的工作人员打算让非非戒烟。但是一下子戒烟是不可能的。开始时，工作人员一天给它十支，后来一天八支、五支，越来越少。非非想吸烟时，工作人员就给它喝牛奶。同时工作人员还告诉大家，非非身体不好，不要再给它烟了。",py:"Dòngwùyuán de gōngzuò rényuán dǎsuan ràng Fēifēi jiè yān. Dànshì yíxiàzi jiè yān shì bù kěnéng de. Kāishǐ shí, gōngzuò rényuán yì tiān gěi tā shí zhī, hòulái yì tiān bā zhī, wǔ zhī, yuèláiyuè shǎo. Fēifēi xiǎng xīyān shí, gōngzuò rényuán jiù gěi tā hē niúnǎi. Tóngshí gōngzuò rényuán hái gàosu dàjiā, Fēifēi shēntǐ bù hǎo, búyào zài gěi tā yān le.",en:"The zoo staff decided to make Feifei quit smoking. But quitting all at once was impossible. At first, the staff gave it ten cigarettes a day, then eight, then five — fewer and fewer. Whenever Feifei wanted to smoke, the staff gave it milk to drink. At the same time, the staff told visitors that Feifei was not well and asked them not to give it any more cigarettes."},{zh:"两个月以后，非非成功地戒了烟。",py:"Liǎng gè yuè yǐhòu, Fēifēi chénggōng de jièle yān.",en:"Two months later, Feifei successfully quit smoking."}],vocab:[{w:"动物园",py:"dòngwùyuán",pos:"n.",en:"zoo"},{w:"黑猩猩",py:"hēixīngxing",pos:"n.",en:"chimpanzee"},{w:"扔",py:"rēng",pos:"v.",en:"throw"},{w:"烟头",py:"yāntóu",pos:"n.",en:"cigarette end"},{w:"吸烟",py:"xīyān",pos:"v.",en:"smoke"},{w:"感冒",py:"gǎnmào",pos:"v.",en:"catch a cold"},{w:"肺炎",py:"fèiyán",pos:"n.",en:"pneumonia"},{w:"人员",py:"rényuán",pos:"n.",en:"personnel, staff"},{w:"戒烟",py:"jièyān",pos:"",en:"quit smoking"},{w:"成功",py:"chénggōng",pos:"adj.",en:"successful"}],points:[{name:"得",en:"get",eg:"在春天，非非感冒了好几次，而且还得了肺炎。",egEn:"In spring, Feifei suffered from flu a couple of times, and got pneumonia.",zh:"“得”，动词。是“得到”的意思，和“失”相对。",enx:"“得” is a verb that means “to get”, opposite to “to lose”.",egs:["（1）这次考试你得了多少分？","（2）经常不吃早饭，容易得病。"]},{name:"打算",en:"plan, consider",eg:"动物园的工作人员打算让非非戒烟。",egEn:"The staff of the zoo planned to make Feifei quit smoking.",zh:"“打算”，动词。是“考虑、计划”的意思。",enx:"“打算” is a verb that means “to think about something and make plans”.",egs:["（1）这个星期天，我打算去爬长城。","（2）你打算什么时候走？"]}],think:["非非是怎么开始吸烟的？","非非又是怎么戒烟的？"],tf:[{q:"非非是动物园的一只黑猩猩。",a:!0},{q:"是动物园的工作人员让非非学习吸烟的。",a:!1},{q:"因为吸烟，所以非非得了肺炎。",a:!0},{q:"非非很容易就戒烟了。",a:!1},{q:"最后非非不吸烟了。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"中国的烟民和禁烟政策",titleEn:"Smokers and Bans on Smoking in China",zh:"以前，中国的烟民很多，人们对吸烟也没有太多限制，在公共场所，不吸烟的人不得不吸“二手烟”。但现在，中国的室内公共场所大多禁止吸烟，法律还规定不得向未成年人售烟，烟草不得进行广告宣传，人们也逐渐意识到吸烟对身体的危害。",en:"There used to be lots of smokers in China, and smoking was not rigidly restricted in public places. Those who did not smoke became victims of “second-hand smoke” against their will. However, nowadays in China, smoking is forbidden in most public indoor places. Laws have been made against selling cigarettes to minors, and cigarettes cannot be advertised. People have gradually become aware of the harm of smoking to health."}},{n:13,title:"一对好朋友：量词和名词",py:"Yí duì hǎo péngyou: liàngcí hé míngcí",en:"Close Companions: Measure Words and Nouns",chars:228,daodu:"每个语言都有名词，可是很多语言没有量词。汉语有很多量词，而且汉语的量词和名词还是一对好朋友。",daoduEn:"Every language has nouns, but many languages don't have measure words. Chinese has lots of measure words, and in Chinese, measure words and nouns are good friends.",paras:[{zh:"汉语的量词常常在名词的前面，量词离不开名词，名词也离不开量词。大家看看我一天的生活就知道了。",py:"Hànyǔ de liàngcí chángcháng zài míngcí de qiánmian, liàngcí líbukāi míngcí, míngcí yě líbukāi liàngcí. Dàjiā kànkan wǒ yì tiān de shēnghuó jiù zhīdào le.",en:"In Chinese, measure words usually come before nouns. Measure words can't do without nouns, and nouns can't do without measure words. Just look at a day in my life and you'll see."},{zh:"我早上七点半起床，先去厨房，喝了一瓶牛奶和一杯咖啡，吃了三片面包和一个苹果，然后回到房间里，穿上一件衣服、一双鞋，背起一个书包（书包里有三本书、两支笔和一个手机）去学校。",py:"Wǒ zǎoshang qī diǎn bàn qǐchuáng, xiān qù chúfáng, hēle yì píng niúnǎi hé yì bēi kāfēi, chī le sān piàn miànbāo hé yí gè píngguǒ, ránhòu huídào fángjiān li, chuānshàng yí jiàn yīfu, yì shuāng xié, bēiqǐ yí gè shūbāo (shūbāo li yǒu sān běn shū, liǎng zhī bǐ hé yí gè shǒujī) qù xuéxiào.",en:"I get up at 7:30 in the morning and go to the kitchen first. I drink a bottle of milk and a cup of coffee, and eat three slices of bread and an apple. Then I go back to my room, put on a top and a pair of shoes, and head to school with a schoolbag on my back (in it are three books, two pens and a cell phone)."},{zh:"在路上，我看到一只可爱的小狗和一只小猫。到了教室，我看见墙上新贴了一张中国地图和一幅画。快上课了，进来一位老师，他戴着一副眼镜。四节课以后我们去食堂吃饭，我要了一瓶啤酒，还有一份西红柿炒鸡蛋。这是我最爱吃的菜。",py:"Zài lùshang, wǒ kàndào yì zhī kě'ài de xiǎo gǒu hé yì zhī xiǎo māo. Dàole jiàoshì, wǒ kànjiàn qiáng shang xīn tiēle yì zhāng Zhōngguó dìtú hé yí fú huà. Kuài shàngkè le, jìnlái yí wèi lǎoshī, tā dàizhe yí fù yǎnjìng. Sì jié kè yǐhòu wǒmen qù shítáng chīfàn, wǒ yàole yì píng píjiǔ, hái yǒu yí fèn Xīhóngshì Chǎo Jīdàn. Zhè shì wǒ zuì ài chī de cài.",en:"On the way, I see a cute little dog and a little cat. When I get to the classroom, I see that a map of China and a painting have just been put up on the wall. Just before class starts, a teacher comes in. He wears a pair of glasses. After four classes, we go to the cafeteria for lunch. I order a bottle of beer and a plate of scrambled eggs with tomatoes. That's my favorite dish."},{zh:"怎么样？汉语的量词和名词是一对好朋友吧。",py:"Zěnmeyàng? Hànyǔ de liàngcí hé míngcí shì yí duì hǎo péngyou ba.",en:"Well? Measure words and nouns in Chinese really are a pair of good friends, aren't they?"}],vocab:[{w:"量词",py:"liàngcí",pos:"n.",en:"measure word"},{w:"前面",py:"qiánmian",pos:"n.",en:"front"},{w:"离不开",py:"líbukāi",pos:"",en:"be inseparable"},{w:"厨房",py:"chúfáng",pos:"n.",en:"kitchen"},{w:"背",py:"bēi",pos:"v.",en:"carry on the back"},{w:"地图",py:"dìtú",pos:"n.",en:"map"},{w:"戴",py:"dài",pos:"v.",en:"wear"},{w:"炒",py:"chǎo",pos:"v.",en:"stir-fry"}],points:[{name:"先……然后……",en:"first ..., then ...",eg:"我……先去厨房……然后回到房间里……",egEn:"First I went into the kitchen, and then came back to the bedroom.",zh:"“先”，副词。表示某一行为或事情发生在前。“然后”，连词。表示一件事情之后接着又发生另一件事情。",enx:"“先” is an adverb that indicates an action or a thing is before another in time. “然后” is a conjunctive word that indicates an event takes place immediately after another.",egs:["（1）下车时，先给司机钱，然后说“谢谢”。","（2）我学汉语的时候，先学拼音，然后学汉字。"]},{name:"快",en:"soon, before long",eg:"快上课了，进来一位老师。",egEn:"When the class was about to begin, a teacher came in.",zh:"“快”，副词。表示将要出现某种情况。“快”作状语时，句末一般有“了”；但“快……的”结构中间不带“了”。",enx:"“快” is an adverb that indicates something will happen in a short time from now. When “快” is used as an adverbial modifier, usually there is “了” at the end of the sentence; but in the structure “快……的”, there is no “了”.",egs:["（1）妈妈说：“赶紧起床！快迟到了！”","（2）天快亮的时候，下雨了。"]},{name:"副",en:"(a) pair of",eg:"他戴着一副眼镜。",egEn:"He wore a pair of glasses.",zh:"“副”，量词。用于成套的东西。",enx:"“副” is a measure word for things that come in pairs.",egs:["（1）每年春节的时候，我家都要贴上一副春联。","（2）我有一副红色的手套（shǒutào: glove），很好看。"]}],think:["“我”的书包里有什么？","教室里有什么？","“我”中午吃了什么？"],tf:[{q:"汉语里的量词要放在名词的前面。",a:!0},{q:"汉语里的名词和量词一般要同时用。",a:!0},{q:"“我”早上吃了一个面包和两片苹果。",a:!1},{q:"教室的墙上有中国地图和北京地图。",a:!1},{q:"六节课以后我们去食堂吃饭。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"汉语的量词",titleEn:"Measure Words in Chinese",zh:"对于留学生来说，汉语的量词又多又难。其实，量词也不是毫无规律的。许多量词本身也是名词，比如“瓶”、“杯”，装在瓶子、杯子里的东西就用这些量词。还有，“双”、“对”、“副”等量词一般用于成套的物品，比如鞋、耳环、手套等。另外，有些量词规定了名词的大小、形状，像“条”、“块”、“片”等。这样记忆量词就容易多了。",en:"There are lots of measure words in Chinese. It is hard for foreign students to learn them. However, there are rules to follow. Many measure words are originally nouns, like “瓶” and “杯”. Things contained in them should be accompanied by measure words “瓶” and “杯”. Additionally, there are other measure words like “双”, “对” and “副”. Generally, they are used when things are in pairs, like shoes, earrings and gloves. There are some measure words that indicate the size and shape of things, like “条”, “块” and “片”. With these rules in mind, it will be much easier to remember these measure words."}},{n:14,title:"十块钱的自行车",py:"Shí kuài qián de zìxíngchē",en:"A Ten-Yuan Bike",chars:257,daodu:"十块钱能买什么呢？能买一辆漂亮的自行车！你相信吗？",daoduEn:"What can ten yuan buy? A beautiful bicycle! Do you believe it?",paras:[{zh:"在一次自行车拍卖会上，有一个小男孩儿总是出价“十块钱”，但是每一次都是别人用一两百元把自行车买走。",py:"Zài yí cì zìxíngchē pāimàihuì shang, yǒu yí gè xiǎo nánháir zǒngshì chūjià “shí kuài qián”, dànshì měi yí cì dōu shì biérén yòng yì-liǎngbǎi yuán bǎ zìxíngchē mǎizǒu.",en:'At a bicycle auction, there was a little boy who always bid "ten yuan". But every time, someone else bought the bike for one or two hundred yuan.'},{zh:"拍卖会中间休息时，拍卖员问那个小男孩儿：“为什么不多出一点儿钱呢？”男孩儿说他只有十块钱。",py:"Pāimàihuì zhōngjiān xiūxi shí, pāimàiyuán wèn nàge xiǎo nánháir: “Wèishénme bù duō chū yìdiǎnr qián ne?” Nánháir shuō tā zhǐ yǒu shí kuài qián.",en:`During the break, the auctioneer asked the little boy, "Why don't you bid a bit more?" The boy said he only had ten yuan.`},{zh:"拍卖会又开始了，男孩儿还是每次只出十块钱，而每次都是别人把自行车买走。后来，大家都注意到这个总是第一个出价的男孩儿。",py:"Pāimàihuì yòu kāishǐ le, nánháir háishi měi cì zhǐ chū shí kuài qián, ér měi cì dōu shì biérén bǎ zìxíngchē mǎizǒu. Hòulái, dàjiā dōu zhùyìdào zhège zǒngshì dì-yī gè chūjià de nánháir.",en:"The auction started again. Each time, the boy still bid only ten yuan, and each time someone else bought the bike. Soon, everyone noticed this boy who was always the first to bid."},{zh:"拍卖会马上要结束了，只剩下最好的一辆自行车。拍卖员问：“谁要出价？”小男孩儿又说：“十块钱！”这一次，没有人出更高的价钱了。拍卖员问了三次都没有人回答，于是他大声宣布：“这辆自行车卖给这个小男孩儿！”这时候，所有的人都站起来鼓掌。小男孩儿拿出手里湿了的十块钱，买了那辆最漂亮的自行车。",py:"Pāimàihuì mǎshàng yào jiéshù le, zhǐ shèngxia zuì hǎo de yí liàng zìxíngchē. Pāimàiyuán wèn: “Shuí yào chūjià?” Xiǎo nánháir yòu shuō: “Shí kuài qián!” Zhè yí cì, méiyǒu rén chū gèng gāo de jiàqián le. Pāimàiyuán wènle sān cì dōu méiyǒu rén huídá, yúshì tā dàshēng xuānbù: “Zhè liàng zìxíngchē màigěi zhège xiǎo nánháir!” Zhè shíhou, suǒyǒu de rén dōu zhàn qǐlai gǔzhǎng. Xiǎo nánháir náchū shǒu li shī le de shí kuài qián, mǎile nà liàng zuì piàoliang de zìxíngchē.",en:'The auction was almost over, and only the best bike was left. The auctioneer asked, "Who would like to bid?" The little boy said again, "Ten yuan!" This time, nobody offered a higher price. The auctioneer asked three times, but no one answered, so he announced loudly, "This bike is sold to this little boy!" At that moment, everyone stood up and clapped. The little boy took out the ten yuan, damp from being held tight in his hand, and bought that most beautiful bike.'}],vocab:[{w:"拍卖",py:"pāimài",pos:"v.",en:"auction"},{w:"注意",py:"zhùyì",pos:"v.",en:"notice"},{w:"价钱",py:"jiàqián",pos:"n.",en:"price"},{w:"宣布",py:"xuānbù",pos:"v.",en:"declare"},{w:"所有",py:"suǒyǒu",pos:"adj.",en:"all"},{w:"鼓掌",py:"gǔzhǎng",pos:"v.",en:"applaud"},{w:"湿",py:"shī",pos:"adj.",en:"wet"}],points:[{name:"总是",en:"always",eg:"有一个小男孩儿总是出价“十块钱”。",egEn:"There was a boy who always offered the price of “ten yuan”.",zh:"“总是”，副词。表示情况、状态持续不变。",enx:"“总是” is an adverb that indicates “the stable duration of a situation or state without any change”.",egs:["（1）老师讲课的时候总是站着，很辛苦。","（2）砍树之前，他总是先磨斧子。"]},{name:"剩下",en:"be left, remain",eg:"拍卖会马上要结束了，只剩下最好的一辆自行车。",egEn:"The auction would be over soon, and there was nothing but the nicest bike left.",zh:"“剩下”，动词。是“去掉一部分之后留下”的意思。",enx:"“剩下” is a verb that means “to be left as a remainder”.",egs:["（1）同学们都走了，教室里只剩下我一个人。","（2）她有 50 元钱，吃饭 30 元，坐车 10 元，还剩下 10 元钱。"]}],think:["大家为什么会注意到这个男孩儿？","为什么小男孩儿手里的十块钱是湿的？"],tf:[{q:"小男孩儿第一个出价，因为先出价可以先买到车。",a:!1},{q:"小男孩儿每次只出十块钱。",a:!0},{q:"小男孩儿买到了拍卖会的最后一辆自行车。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"拍卖会上，一辆自行车的价钱一般是（　）。",options:["一两百元","十块钱","几十块钱","一千多元"],answer:0},{q:"为什么拍卖最后一辆自行车时，没有人出比小男孩儿更高的价钱？因为（　）。",options:["最后一辆自行车不好","大家都没有钱了","拍卖员没有看见别人","大家都想让小男孩儿买到这辆车"],answer:3},{q:"小男孩儿买到车时，所有人都站起来鼓掌，是因为（　）。",options:["拍卖会结束了","那辆自行车非常漂亮","大家为小男孩儿感到高兴","拍卖员说得很好"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"中国的拍卖业",titleEn:"Auction Business in China",zh:"1986 年，随着第一家国有拍卖行在广州成立，在中国中断了近三十年的拍卖业进入恢复、试点阶段，各类拍卖行如雨后春笋般地出现在中华大地，且逐渐形成规模。1994 年，两大国际拍卖公司——苏富比和佳士得先后在上海设立了办事处，进一步刺激了中国的拍卖业，促进了该行业的迅速发展。",en:"The auction business in China, suspended for nearly 30 years, was restored in 1986. Since the first state-owned auction house was set up in Guangzhou, various auction companies have sprung up all over China and grown into big businesses. In 1994, two international auction companies, Sotheby's and Christie's, opened their offices in Shanghai. They have pushed forward China's auction business and promoted the rapid development of this industry."}},{n:15,title:"聪明的男孩儿",py:"Cōngming de nánháir",en:"A Clever Boy",chars:240,daodu:"当你爱上一个人时，你会怎么做？下面的方法怎么样？大家学习一下吧！",daoduEn:"When you fall in love with someone, what do you do? How about the method below? Let's learn from it!",paras:[{zh:"一个大学生爱上了一个女孩儿。这天，他勇敢地跟她打了一个招呼。他对女孩儿说：“我在纸上写了一句话。如果我写的是事实，你就送给我一张你的照片，好吗？”",py:"Yí gè dàxuésheng àishàngle yí gè nǚháir. Zhè tiān, tā yǒnggǎn de gēn tā dǎle yí gè zhāohu. Tā duì nǚháir shuō: “Wǒ zài zhǐ shang xiěle yí jù huà. Rúguǒ wǒ xiě de shì shìshí, nǐ jiù sònggěi wǒ yì zhāng nǐ de zhàopiàn, hǎo ma?”",en:`A college student fell in love with a girl. One day, he bravely went up and said hello to her. He said to the girl, "I've written a sentence on a piece of paper. If what I wrote is true, will you give me a photo of yourself?"`},{zh:"女孩儿不愿意把照片送给他，心想：无论他写什么，我都说不是事实，看他怎么办。所以女孩儿就说：“好的。”",py:"Nǚháir bú yuànyì bǎ zhàopiàn sònggěi tā, xīnxiǎng: wúlùn tā xiě shénme, wǒ dōu shuō bú shì shìshí, kàn tā zěnme bàn. Suǒyǐ nǚháir jiù shuō: “Hǎode.”",en:`The girl didn't want to give him her photo. She thought, "Whatever he writes, I'll just say it isn't true, and we'll see what he does then." So she said, "OK."`},{zh:"“如果我说的不是事实，你就不要把照片给我。”男孩儿说。",py:"“Rúguǒ wǒ shuō de bú shì shìshí, nǐ jiù búyào bǎ zhàopiàn gěi wǒ.” Nánháir shuō.",en:`"And if what I wrote isn't true, then don't give me the photo," the boy said.`},{zh:"“那当然！”女孩儿回答。",py:"“Nà dāngrán!” Nǚháir huídá.",en:'"Of course!" the girl replied.'},{zh:"男孩儿高兴地说：“好！”然后给了她一张纸条。",py:"Nánháir gāoxìng de shuō: “Hǎo!” Ránhòu gěile tā yì zhāng zhǐtiáo.",en:'The boy said happily, "Great!" Then he handed her a note.'},{zh:"看了纸条上的话，女孩儿想了半天也想不出更好的办法，最后只好给了他一张照片。",py:"Kànle zhǐtiáo shang de huà, nǚháir xiǎngle bàntiān yě xiǎng bù chū gèng hǎo de bànfǎ, zuìhòu zhǐhǎo gěile tā yì zhāng zhàopiàn.",en:"After reading the note, the girl thought for a long time but couldn't find a way out. In the end, she had no choice but to give him a photo."},{zh:"聪明的男孩儿写了什么呢？他写了很简单的一句话：“你不会吻我，也不会给我你的照片。”后来，女孩儿跟男孩儿结婚了，他们生活得很幸福。",py:"Cōngming de nánháir xiěle shénme ne? Tā xiěle hěn jiǎndān de yí jù huà: “Nǐ bú huì wěn wǒ, yě bú huì gěi wǒ nǐ de zhàopiàn.” Hòulái, nǚháir gēn nánháir jiéhūn le, tāmen shēnghuó de hěn xìngfú.",en:`What did the clever boy write? Just one simple sentence: "You won't kiss me, and you won't give me your photo." Later, the girl married the boy, and they lived very happily.`}],vocab:[{w:"勇敢",py:"yǒnggǎn",pos:"adj.",en:"brave"},{w:"事实",py:"shìshí",pos:"n.",en:"truth"},{w:"纸条",py:"zhǐtiáo",pos:"n.",en:"paper slip"},{w:"半天",py:"bàntiān",pos:"n.",en:"a long time, quite a while"},{w:"办法",py:"bànfǎ",pos:"n.",en:"idea, method"},{w:"聪明",py:"cōngming",pos:"adj.",en:"clever"},{w:"结婚",py:"jiéhūn",pos:"v.",en:"marry, get married"},{w:"幸福",py:"xìngfú",pos:"adj.",en:"happy"}],points:[{name:"打招呼",en:"greet, say hello (to)",eg:"这天，他勇敢地跟她打了一个招呼。",egEn:"One day, he greeted her bravely.",zh:"“打招呼”，指用言语或动作对人表示问候。",enx:"“打招呼” means “to greet somebody with words or movements”.",egs:["（1）你一般怎么和别人打招呼？","（2）妹妹很懂礼貌，在学校经常跟老师打招呼。"]},{name:"无论……都……",en:"... whatever ...",eg:"无论他写什么，我都说不是事实。",egEn:"No matter what he wrote, I would say it was not true.",zh:"“无论……都……”，表示在任何条件下，结果都不会改变。",enx:"“无论……都……” is a structure used to express no matter what happens, the result will not change.",egs:["（1）无论我怎么问，他都不回答。","（2）无论你有没有钱，我都爱你。"]},{name:"只好",en:"have to",eg:"女孩儿……最后只好给了他一张照片。",egEn:"Finally, the girl had no choice but to hand over her photo to him.",zh:"“只好”，副词。表示不得不，没有别的选择。“只好”用在复句的后一个分句中，两个分句的主语相同时，只能用在主语后面。",enx:"“只好” is an adverb that means “have to, or have no choice but to”. “只好” is usually put in the second clause of a compound sentence. When the two clauses have the same subject, “只好” should be put after the subject.",egs:["（1）别人都不去，只好我去。","（2）下雨了，不能出去，我们只好在家里上网聊天儿。"]}],think:["女孩儿开始的时候愿意给男孩儿照片吗？","男孩儿用什么办法得到了女孩儿的照片？","最后女孩儿喜欢男孩儿了吗？"],tf:[{q:"女孩儿说“好的”，因为她想给男孩儿照片。",a:!1},{q:"男孩儿觉得，他最后肯定能得到照片。",a:!0},{q:"男孩儿非常聪明。",a:!0},{q:"无论女孩儿回答什么，最后她都要给男孩儿照片。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"中国人婚恋方式的变化",titleEn:"Changes in How the Chinese Get Married",zh:"文中的男孩儿可以勇敢地去追求自己喜爱的人，但在古代的中国，男女想要相识恋爱可没这么简单。双方一般都需通过媒人介绍才能了解对方的情况，有的人结婚后才知道对方的长相。后来发展到先通过媒人介绍，彼此觉得条件相当后再见面相亲。20世纪上半叶开始提倡“恋爱自由”，年轻男女都愿意自己去追求幸福，曾一度盛行的相亲逐渐被人冷落。不过如今，由于大家工作忙碌，越来越多的人又开始重新选择相亲的方式了。",en:"The boy in the story can bravely court the girl he loves. However, in ancient China, it was not easy for boys and girls to get acquainted for marriage. Generally, the two sides could only get to know each other through the introduction of a matchmaker. Some did not have a chance to know what their future spouse looked like until after the wedding time. Later, things changed a little. A girl and a boy could get to know each other through a matchmaker first. If they felt mutually satisfied, they would date each other. In the first half of the 20th century, “Free Love” was advocated. Young boys and girls chose to seek love by themselves. The practice of “arranged date” gradually lost its popularity. Nowadays, due to busy work schedules, more and more people return to the old way of arranged date."}},{n:16,title:"哪里哪里",py:"Nǎli nǎli",en:"Where Where",chars:229,daodu:"中国人学外语、外国人学汉语都会有很多问题。除了语音、词汇、语法的困难以外，有时候还有文化上的问题。",daoduEn:"Chinese people learning foreign languages and foreigners learning Chinese both run into lots of problems. Besides pronunciation, vocabulary and grammar, there are sometimes cultural problems too.",paras:[{zh:"有一个英国人，他在中国生活了半年，学了一点儿汉语。",py:"Yǒu yí gè Yīngguórén, tā zài Zhōngguó shēnghuóle bàn nián, xuéle yìdiǎnr Hànyǔ.",en:"There was an Englishman who had lived in China for half a year and learned a little Chinese."},{zh:"有一次，这位先生和他的妻子一起参加一个中国朋友的婚礼。婚礼是在一家大饭店举行的。那一天，新郎和新娘非常热情。英国太太是第一次和新娘见面。她握着新娘的手，用英语对她的先生说：“她是我见过的最漂亮的中国姑娘！”这位英国先生翻译了这句话。新郎听了，很高兴。他礼貌地说：“哪里哪里。”",py:"Yǒu yí cì, zhè wèi xiānsheng hé tā de qīzi yìqǐ cānjiā yí gè Zhōngguó péngyou de hūnli. Hūnli shì zài yì jiā dà fàndiàn jǔxíng de. Nà yì tiān, xīnláng hé xīnniáng fēicháng rèqíng. Yīngguó tàitai shì dì-yī cì hé xīnniáng jiànmiàn. Tā wòzhe xīnniáng de shǒu, yòng Yīngyǔ duì tā de xiānsheng shuō: “Tā shì wǒ jiànguo de zuì piàoliang de Zhōngguó gūniang!” Zhè wèi Yīngguó xiānsheng fānyìle zhè jù huà. Xīnláng tīng le, hěn gāoxìng. Tā lǐmào de shuō: “Nǎli nǎli.”",en:`Once, this gentleman and his wife went to a Chinese friend's wedding. The wedding was held in a big hotel. That day, the bride and groom were very warm and welcoming. It was the English wife's first time meeting the bride. Holding the bride's hand, she said to her husband in English, "She's the most beautiful Chinese girl I've ever seen!" The Englishman translated this. The groom was very pleased and said politely, "Nǎli nǎli" (literally "where, where" — a modest way of saying "Oh, not at all").`},{zh:"英国先生学汉语的时间不长，还不知道这句话是什么意思，就翻译为：“Where? Where?”英国太太一听，觉得很奇怪，心想：怎么？还要我说出她哪儿漂亮吗？她不知道应该怎样回答，只好对她丈夫说：“你告诉他，他的妻子全身上下都很漂亮。”",py:"Yīngguó xiānsheng xué Hànyǔ de shíjiān bù cháng, hái bù zhīdào zhè jù huà shì shénme yìsi, jiù fānyì wéi: “Where? Where?” Yīngguó tàitai yì tīng, juéde hěn qíguài, xīnxiǎng: zěnme? Hái yào wǒ shuōchū tā nǎr piàoliang ma? Tā bù zhīdào yīnggāi zěnyàng huídá, zhǐhǎo duì tā zhàngfu shuō: “Nǐ gàosu tā, tā de qīzi quánshēn shàng-xià dōu hěn piàoliang.”",en:`The Englishman hadn't been learning Chinese for long and didn't know what this phrase meant, so he translated it as: "Where? Where?" His wife found this very strange and thought, "What? He wants me to say exactly where she's beautiful?" Not knowing how to answer, she could only say to her husband, "Tell him his wife is beautiful from head to toe."`}],vocab:[{w:"妻子",py:"qīzi",pos:"n.",en:"wife"},{w:"参加",py:"cānjiā",pos:"v.",en:"participate in, take part in"},{w:"婚礼",py:"hūnli",pos:"n.",en:"wedding"},{w:"举行",py:"jǔxíng",pos:"v.",en:"hold (a meeting, ceremony, etc.)"},{w:"新郎",py:"xīnláng",pos:"n.",en:"bridegroom"},{w:"新娘",py:"xīnniáng",pos:"n.",en:"bride"},{w:"握",py:"wò",pos:"v.",en:"shake hands, hold"},{w:"礼貌",py:"lǐmào",pos:"adj.",en:"polite"},{w:"全身",py:"quánshēn",pos:"n.",en:"from head to foot, whole body"}],points:[{name:"一点儿",en:"some, a little",eg:"他在中国生活了半年，学了一点儿汉语。",egEn:"He had been living in China for half a year, and had learnt a little Chinese.",zh:"“一点儿”，表示数量很少，修饰名词。",enx:"“一点儿” means “a little”. It is used to modify a noun.",egs:["（1）我喝咖啡的时候喜欢放一点儿糖。","（2）他喝了一点儿水。"]},{name:"是……的",en:"It is ... that ...",eg:"婚礼是在一家大饭店举行的。",egEn:"The wedding ceremony was held in a grand hotel.",zh:"“是……的”句，用来强调与某个已经发生或完成的动作有关的某一方面，如时间、地点、方式等。",enx:"“是……的” is used to emphasize a certain aspect, like time, place or manner, of an action that has happened or finished.",egs:["（1）爸爸是晚上七点回家的。","（2）玛丽是坐飞机回国的。"]}],think:["那个英国先生的汉语怎么样？","“哪里哪里”是什么意思？应该怎么用？"],tf:[{q:"英国先生知道“哪里哪里”是什么意思。",a:!1},{q:"英国太太会说一点儿汉语。",a:!1},{q:"英国先生的翻译是对的。",a:!1},{q:"新郎想知道新娘哪里漂亮。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"不同寻常的“哪里”",titleEn:"The Unusual “哪里”",zh:"有些中国话字面上的意思与实际表达的内容不相符。比如“哪里哪里”，实际上表示对别人称赞的一种谦虚，并不是真的询问地点。当你觉得麻烦了别人，表示感谢时，对方也可能会说“哪儿的话”，也就是“不用客气”。另外，中国人打招呼有时会问“你去哪里呀？”，这并不是探究你的隐私，真关心你要去哪里，而只是很随意的一种打招呼的方式。你可以含糊地回答“出去一下”就行。",en:"Some terms in Chinese are inconsistent in their literal meanings and their actual meanings. For example, “哪里哪里” is actually a modest reply to others' compliments, rather than a query of location. When you feel you have bothered someone and have expressed your thanks, the other side may say “哪儿的话”, which means “不用客气” (my pleasure). Additionally, when the Chinese greet each other, they may ask the question “你去哪里呀?”. As a matter of fact, he/she does not intend to ask about where you are heading since it is your privacy. It is just a casual way of greeting others, and it is enough for you to reply vaguely with “出去一下”."}},{n:17,title:"三个小板凳",py:"Sān gè xiǎo bǎndèng",en:"Three Little Stools",chars:213,daodu:"爱因斯坦（Albert Einstein）的第三个小板凳还是不太好看，但已经比前两个小板凳好多了！",daoduEn:"Einstein's third little stool still wasn't very pretty, but it was much better than the first two!",paras:[{zh:"爱因斯坦在上小学的时候，老师和同学都认为他是一个很笨的学生。有一天，老师让每个人回家做一件作品，第二天交给她。",py:"Àiyīnsītǎn zài shàng xiǎoxué de shíhou, lǎoshī hé tóngxué dōu rènwéi tā shì yí gè hěn bèn de xuésheng. Yǒu yì tiān, lǎoshī ràng měi gè rén huíjiā zuò yí jiàn zuòpǐn, dì-èr tiān jiāogěi tā.",en:"When Einstein was in primary school, his teacher and classmates all thought he was a very slow student. One day, the teacher asked everyone to make something at home and hand it in the next day."},{zh:"第二天，同学们都带来了自己的作品，有文具盒，有布娃娃，还有很多漂亮的玩具。当爱因斯坦把自己的作品——一个非常难看的小板凳交给老师的时候，教室里发出了嘲笑的声音。",py:"Dì-èr tiān, tóngxuémen dōu dàiláile zìjǐ de zuòpǐn, yǒu wénjùhé, yǒu bùwáwa, hái yǒu hěn duō piàoliang de wánjù. Dāng Àiyīnsītǎn bǎ zìjǐ de zuòpǐn —— yí gè fēicháng nánkàn de xiǎo bǎndèng jiāogěi lǎoshī de shíhou, jiàoshì li fāchūle cháoxiào de shēngyīn.",en:"The next day, all the students brought in what they had made: pencil boxes, cloth dolls, and lots of pretty toys. When Einstein handed in his — a very ugly little stool — the classroom filled with mocking laughter."},{zh:"“哦，上帝，世界上还有比这更难看的东西吗？”老师摇摇头说。",py:"“Ò, Shàngdì, shìjiè shang hái yǒu bǐ zhè gèng nánkàn de dōngxi ma?” Lǎoshī yáoyao tóu shuō.",en:'"Oh, God! Could there be anything in the world uglier than this?" the teacher said, shaking her head.'},{zh:"“有。”爱因斯坦又拿出两个更难看的小板凳，“这是第一次做的，这是第二次做的，刚才交上去的是第三次做的。虽然不好看，但是它比这两个好很多了。”",py:"“Yǒu.” Àiyīnsītǎn yòu náchū liǎng gè gèng nánkàn de xiǎo bǎndèng, “Zhè shì dì-yī cì zuò de, zhè shì dì-èr cì zuò de, gāngcái jiāo shàngqu de shì dì-sān cì zuò de. Suīrán bù hǎokàn, dànshì tā bǐ zhè liǎng gè hǎo hěn duō le.”",en:`"Yes." Einstein took out two even uglier little stools. "This is the one I made the first time, and this is the one I made the second time. The one I just handed in is my third try. It's not pretty, but it's much better than these two."`},{zh:"这时，教室里安静了下来。",py:"Zhèshí, jiàoshì li ānjìngle xiàlái.",en:"At that, the classroom went quiet."}],vocab:[{w:"笨",py:"bèn",pos:"adj.",en:"stupid"},{w:"作品",py:"zuòpǐn",pos:"n.",en:"works (of literature and art)"},{w:"交",py:"jiāo",pos:"v.",en:"hand in"},{w:"玩具",py:"wánjù",pos:"n.",en:"toy"},{w:"难看",py:"nánkàn",pos:"adj.",en:"ugly"},{w:"板凳",py:"bǎndèng",pos:"n.",en:"stool"},{w:"发出",py:"fāchū",pos:"v.",en:"send out (sound, light, or signals)"},{w:"嘲笑",py:"cháoxiào",pos:"v.",en:"laugh at, ridicule"},{w:"上帝",py:"Shàngdì",pos:"n.",en:"God"},{w:"安静",py:"ānjìng",pos:"adj.",en:"quiet"}],points:[{name:"比",en:"than",eg:"世界上还有比这更难看的东西吗？",egEn:"Is there anything uglier than this in the world?",zh:"“比”，介词。用于比较。“比”的前面和后面的词，词类或结构一般相同，但有的也可以省略，以避免重复。",enx:"“比” is an preposition used for making comparisons. The components before and after it should be of the same part of speech or the same structure, though omission is possible to avoid repetition.",egs:["（1）新郎（170厘米）比新娘（165厘米）高。","（2）肯德基卖的油条比中国饭馆的贵。"]},{name:"虽然……但是……",en:"although ...",eg:"虽然不好看，但是它比这两个要好很多了。",egEn:"Although it did not look nice, it was much better than the other two.",zh:"“虽然……但是……”，表示转折关系。“虽然”引导的从句表示承认某种情况为事实，“但是”表示转折。",enx:"“虽然……但是……” indicates adversative relations. “虽然” introduces a clause that indicates “the acknowledgement of some facts”, while “但是” indicates “transition”.",egs:["（1）老师虽然快六十了，但是看上去像四十多岁。","（2）虽然他才学了半年汉语，但是他已经说得很好了。"]}],think:["老师让每个人回家做什么？","老师觉得爱因斯坦的作品怎么样？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"爱因斯坦上小学时，老师和同学认为他（　）。",options:["很聪明","很笨","很漂亮","很努力"],answer:1},{q:"文中没有提到的作品是（　）。",options:["文具盒","布娃娃","小板凳","书包"],answer:3},{q:"同学们都嘲笑爱因斯坦，因为他的小板凳（　）。",options:["太小了","非常难看","不是他自己做的","做得太慢了"],answer:1},{q:"教室里的安静说明大家（　）。",options:["明白了爱因斯坦一直在努力","都觉得小板凳很好看","都不喜欢爱因斯坦","还在嘲笑他"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"好孩子是夸出来的",titleEn:"Commendation Helps Kids Grow",zh:"鼓励和赞美是教育孩子的重要方式。用这种方式来教育孩子，往往会收到事半功倍的效果。然而，鼓励并不只是简单的表扬。父母需要多发现孩子的优点，多从正面的角度来欣赏和赞美，从而让孩子树立自信。当然，鼓励还要讲究好分寸，把握好尺度，这样才能使家长的有意引导和孩子的自主发展达到和谐统一。所以，如果学会欣赏孩子、鼓励孩子、赞美孩子，那么再普通的孩子也能创造奇迹。",en:"Encouragement and praise are two important ways to educate children. They usually get better results with less effort. However, encouragement does not simply mean praise. Parents should find more about their strong points, appreciate and praise them to boost their confidence. However, do not go too far in praising. Only in this way can parents’ guide interact in harmony with children’s self-development. If you know how to appreciate, encourage and praise your kids, even a common child can make wonders."}},{n:18,title:"东方小巨人——姚明",py:"Dōngfāng xiǎo jùrén —— Yáo Míng",en:"Yao Ming, a New Asian Star",chars:300,daodu:"你喜欢运动吗？你喜欢的体育明星（míngxīng：star）是谁？你知道哪些中国的体育明星？",daoduEn:"Do you like sports? Who is your favorite sports star? Which Chinese sports stars do you know?",paras:[{zh:"姚明是中国人都知道的运动员。他一九八零年九月十二日出生在上海，身高二点二六米，体重一百四十一千克。姚明的父母都曾经是篮球运动员，父亲身高二点零八米，母亲身高一点八八米。",py:"Yáo Míng shì Zhōngguórén dōu zhīdào de yùndòngyuán. Tā yī jiǔ bā líng nián jiǔ yuè shí'èr rì chūshēng zài Shànghǎi, shēngāo èr diǎn èr liù mǐ, tǐzhòng yìbǎi sìshíyī qiānkè. Yáo Míng de fù-mǔ dōu céngjīng shì lánqiú yùndòngyuán, fùqīn shēngāo èr diǎn líng bā mǐ, mǔqīn shēngāo yī diǎn bā bā mǐ.",en:"Yao Ming is an athlete every Chinese person knows. He was born in Shanghai on September 12, 1980. He is 2.26 meters tall and weighs 141 kilograms. Both of Yao Ming's parents used to be basketball players: his father is 2.08 meters tall and his mother 1.88 meters."},{zh:"姚明在四岁生日时，得到了第一个篮球。六岁时，他看了美国篮球队在上海的表演，开始知道NBA。九岁那年，姚明开始篮球训练，而且非常努力。因为爸爸妈妈都打篮球，所以他在篮球方面很有天赋。十八岁时，他就进入了中国国家队。",py:"Yáo Míng zài sì suì shēngrì shí, dédàole dì-yī gè lánqiú. Liù suì shí, tā kànle Měiguó lánqiúduì zài Shànghǎi de biǎoyǎn, kāishǐ zhīdào NBA. Jiǔ suì nà nián, Yáo Míng kāishǐ lánqiú xùnliàn, érqiě fēicháng nǔlì. Yīnwèi bàba māma dōu dǎ lánqiú, suǒyǐ tā zài lánqiú fāngmiàn hěn yǒu tiānfù. Shí-bā suì shí, tā jiù jìnrùle Zhōngguó Guójiāduì.",en:"Yao Ming got his first basketball on his fourth birthday. At six, he watched an American basketball team play in Shanghai and first learned about the NBA. At nine, he started basketball training and worked very hard. Because both his mom and dad played basketball, he had a real gift for the game. At eighteen, he joined China's national team."},{zh:"二零零零年奥运会，姚明的篮球打得非常好。二零零二年六月，姚明加入美国休斯敦火箭队，成为第三位加入NBA的中国球员。现在越来越多的外国人称姚明是“东方小巨人”。二零零七年，美国《时代》杂志把姚明作为中国人的代表，介绍了中国的发展。二零零八年八月，姚明和其他中国队员一起，在北京奥运会上也取得了不错的成绩。",py:"Èr líng líng líng nián Àoyùnhuì, Yáo Míng de lánqiú dǎ de fēicháng hǎo. Èr líng líng èr nián liù yuè, Yáo Míng jiārù Měiguó Xiūsīdùn Huǒjiànduì, chéngwéi dì-sān wèi jiārù NBA de Zhōngguó qiúyuán. Xiànzài yuèláiyuè duō de wàiguórén chēng Yáo Míng shì “dōngfāng xiǎo jùrén”. Èr líng líng qī nián, Měiguó 《Shídài》 zázhì bǎ Yáo Míng zuòwéi Zhōngguórén de dàibiǎo, jièshàole Zhōngguó de fāzhǎn. Èr líng líng bā nián bā yuè, Yáo Míng hé qítā Zhōngguó duìyuán yìqǐ, zài Běijīng Àoyùnhuì shang yě qǔdéle búcuò de chéngjì.",en:`At the 2000 Olympics, Yao Ming played excellent basketball. In June 2002, he joined the Houston Rockets in the United States, becoming the third Chinese player in the NBA. Now more and more people abroad call Yao Ming the "Little Giant of the East". In 2007, America's Time magazine featured Yao Ming as a representative of the Chinese people to show China's development. In August 2008, Yao Ming and his Chinese teammates also did well at the Beijing Olympics.`}],vocab:[{w:"运动员",py:"yùndòngyuán",pos:"n.",en:"sportsman, athlete"},{w:"队",py:"duì",pos:"n.",en:"team"},{w:"表演",py:"biǎoyǎn",pos:"v.",en:"perform"},{w:"训练",py:"xùnliàn",pos:"v.",en:"train, drill"},{w:"努力",py:"nǔlì",pos:"adj.",en:"hardworking, diligent"},{w:"天赋",py:"tiānfù",pos:"n.",en:"gift, talent"},{w:"奥运会",py:"Àoyùnhuì",pos:"n.",en:"Olympic Games"},{w:"加入",py:"jiārù",pos:"v.",en:"join"},{w:"称",py:"chēng",pos:"v.",en:"call"},{w:"巨人",py:"jùrén",pos:"n.",en:"giant"},{w:"介绍",py:"jièshào",pos:"v.",en:"introduce"}],points:[{name:"曾经",en:"once, before",eg:"姚明的父母都曾经是篮球运动员。",egEn:"Yao Ming's parents used to be basketball players.",zh:"“曾经”，副词。表示以前发生过某种情况或有过某种行为。“曾经”后面的动词常帮助词“过”。",enx:"“曾经” is an adverb that indicates “something happened in the past”. The auxiliary word “过” usually accompanies verbs after “曾经”.",egs:["（1）爸爸曾经很喜欢吸烟，现在戒烟了。","（2）来中国留学以前，我曾经学过半年汉语。"]},{name:"成为",en:"become",eg:"姚明加入美国休斯敦火箭队，成为第三位加入NBA的中国球员。",egEn:"Yao Ming joined Houston Rockets in the United States, becoming the third Chinese basketball player in NBA.",zh:"“成为”，动词。表示从一种情况、状态变成另一种情况、状态。",enx:"“成为” is a verb that indicates “shifting from one situation or state to another”.",egs:["（1）妈妈24岁时成为了一位老师。","（2）小时候，我想成为一个空姐（kōngjiě：air hostess）。"]},{name:"作为",en:"as, in the role of",eg:"美国《时代》杂志把姚明作为中国人的代表，介绍了中国的发展。",egEn:"American magazine Time selected Yao Ming as a representative of the Chinese to introduce the development of China.",zh:"“作为”，动词。表示“当作”或“从人的某种身份或事物的某种性质来说”的意思。",enx:"“作为” is a verb that means “regard as” or “from the perspective of someone's social status or the nature of something”.",egs:["（1）今天山本作为我们班的代表参加了留学生表演。","（2）我认为，作为一个学生，学习是最重要的。"]}],think:["姚明是哪里人？","外国人称姚明是什么？"],tf:[{q:"姚明的身高是2.08米。",a:!1},{q:"姚明4岁的时候第一次知道NBA。",a:!1},{q:"姚明18岁的时候进入中国国家队。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"姚明在篮球方面很有天赋，因为（　）。",options:["他的爸爸妈妈都打篮球","他四岁就有了篮球","他看过美国篮球队的表演","他九岁开始训练"],answer:0},{q:"在姚明之前，NBA有（　）个中国球员。",options:["一","两","三","四"],answer:1},{q:"姚明被写入《时代》杂志那年（　）岁。",options:["二十二","二十五","二十七","二十九"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"篮球运动在中国",titleEn:"Basketball in China",zh:"篮球在中国是仅次于乒乓球的大众球类运动，尤其受到年轻人的欢迎。对中国人来说，篮球除了有健身功能以外，还有娱乐作用。美国NBA和中国CBA等职业篮球赛一直是高收视率的节目，“街头篮球”也日渐流行。如今，已有多名中国篮球运动员到美国等篮球强国打球，中国篮球与世界的联系越来越密切了。",en:"Basketball is the second most popular game next to table tennis in China, particularly loved by the youth. To the Chinese, basketball game is an entertainment as well as a physical exercise. TV programmes of professional basketball games like NBA of the United States and CBA of China have always enjoyed high audience ratings. Street basketball is also getting increasingly popular. Several Chinese basketball players have joined top teams in countries like the United States. The Chinese basketball has become more and more closely related to the outside world."}},{n:19,title:"马的眼睛怎么了？",py:"Mǎ de yǎnjing zěnme le?",en:"What Is the Matter with the Horse's Eyes?",chars:164,daodu:"怎样聪明地对付（duìfu: deal with）坏人？看看张三是怎么做的。",daoduEn:"How can you deal cleverly with a bad person? Let's see how Zhang San did it.",paras:[{zh:"一次，邻居偷走了张三的马。张三和警察一起在邻居的家里找到了马，可是邻居不愿意把马交出来。张三用手把马的双眼捂住说：“如果这马是你的，那么，你说它的哪只眼睛是瞎的？”",py:"Yí cì, línjū tōuzǒule Zhāng Sān de mǎ. Zhāng Sān hé jǐngchá yìqǐ zài línjū de jiāli zhǎodàole mǎ, kěshì línjū bú yuànyì bǎ mǎ jiāo chūlái. Zhāng Sān yòng shǒu bǎ mǎ de shuāngyǎn wǔzhù shuō: “Rúguǒ zhè mǎ shì nǐ de, nàme, nǐ shuō tā de nǎ zhī yǎnjing shì xiā de?”",en:`Once, a neighbor stole Zhang San's horse. Zhang San and a policeman found the horse at the neighbor's house, but the neighbor refused to hand it over. Zhang San covered both of the horse's eyes with his hands and said, "If this horse is yours, then tell me: which of its eyes is blind?"`},{zh:"“右眼。”邻居回答说。",py:"“Yòuyǎn.” Línjū huídá shuō.",en:'"The right eye," the neighbor answered.'},{zh:"张三把手从右眼移开，马的右眼一点儿问题都没有。",py:"Zhāng Sān bǎ shǒu cóng yòuyǎn yíkāi, mǎ de yòuyǎn yìdiǎnr wèntí dōu méiyǒu.",en:"Zhang San took his hand away from the right eye. There was nothing wrong with the horse's right eye at all."},{zh:"“啊，我弄错了，”邻居赶忙说，“是左眼！”",py:"“À, wǒ nòngcuò le,” Línjū gǎnmáng shuō, “Shì zuǒyǎn!”",en:`"Oh, I got it wrong," the neighbor said quickly. "It's the left eye!"`},{zh:"张三把左手移开，马的左眼也没有问题。",py:"Zhāng Sān bǎ zuǒshǒu yíkāi, mǎ de zuǒyǎn yě méiyǒu wèntí.",en:"Zhang San took away his left hand. There was nothing wrong with the horse's left eye either."},{zh:"“对不起！我又说错了。”邻居为自己辩护说。",py:"“Duìbuqǐ! Wǒ yòu shuōcuò le.” Línjū wèi zìjǐ biànhù shuō.",en:'"Sorry! I got it wrong again," the neighbor said, trying to defend himself.'},{zh:"“够了够了！”警察说，“这完全可以证明马不是你的！”",py:"“Gòu le gòu le!” Jǐngchá shuō, “Zhè wánquán kěyǐ zhèngmíng mǎ bú shì nǐ de!”",en:`"Enough, enough!" said the policeman. "This proves the horse isn't yours!"`}],vocab:[{w:"邻居",py:"línjū",pos:"n.",en:"neighbour"},{w:"偷",py:"tōu",pos:"v.",en:"steal"},{w:"警察",py:"jǐngchá",pos:"n.",en:"policeman"},{w:"捂住",py:"wǔzhù",pos:"",en:"cover, muffle"},{w:"瞎",py:"xiā",pos:"v.",en:"blind"},{w:"移开",py:"yíkāi",pos:"",en:"remove"},{w:"辩护",py:"biànhù",pos:"v.",en:"defend"}],points:[{name:"赶忙",en:"hurriedly, make haste",eg:"“啊，我弄错了，”邻居赶忙说，“是左眼！”",egEn:"“Ah, I have got it wrong,” the neighbour added immediately, “It is the left eye!”",zh:"“赶忙”，副词。意思是“连忙，很急地（做一件事）”。",enx:"“赶忙” is an adverb that means “immediately, anxiously (do something)”.",egs:["（1）听到有人叫她，她赶忙跑出来。","（2）已经八点了，我赶忙起床。"]},{name:"证明",en:"prove, testify to",eg:"这完全可以证明马不是你的！",egEn:"This can totally prove the horse is not yours!",zh:"“证明”，动词。指用材料等说明人的身份或事物是真实的，观点、看法等是正确的。",enx:"“证明” is a verb that means “to prove the authenticity of one’s identity or a fact, or one’s viewpoint or opinion is correct”.",egs:["（1）你说你昨天生病了，谁能证明呢？","（2）事实证明我是对的，她说谎了。"]}],think:["张三怎么证明邻居偷了他的马？","警察的结论是什么？"],tf:[{q:"马的一只眼睛看不见东西。",a:!1},{q:"邻居不知道那匹马是谁的。",a:!1},{q:"邻居不知道马的眼睛瞎不瞎。",a:!0},{q:"张三的邻居是个小偷。",a:!0},{q:"那匹马是张三的。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"马在中国文化中的形象",titleEn:"Horse’s Image in the Chinese Culture",zh:"马在中国文化中被赋予了许多正面的品格。首先，马对主人非常忠诚。其次，马能够任劳任怨，忍辱负重，并且非常有战斗力。此外，马还被认为是很智慧的动物。中国人就把那些特别有才能的人称为“千里马”。",en:"The horse is considered a symbol of many good morals in the Chinese culture. First, it is very loyal to its master. Second, it can work hard, shoulder pressure and humiliation, and has fighting vitality. Additionally, horses are considered a wise animal. The Chinese call people of great talent “千里马” (horses that can cover a thousand li a day)."}},{n:20,title:"有趣的心理测试",py:"Yǒuqù de xīnlǐ cèshì",en:"An Interesting Psychological Test",chars:278,daodu:"你关心家人吗？你喜欢跟朋友一起玩儿吗？你觉得钱重要吗？做完下面的心理测试，你就能知道答案了。",daoduEn:"Do you care about your family? Do you like spending time with friends? Do you think money is important? Take the psychological test below and you'll find out.",paras:[{zh:"有这样一个心理测试：你一个人在家，突然同时发生五件事，你该怎么办？",py:"Yǒu zhèyàng yí gè xīnlǐ cèshì: nǐ yí gè rén zàijiā, tūrán tóngshí fāshēng wǔ jiàn shì, nǐ gāi zěnme bàn?",en:"Here's a psychological test: You're home alone, and suddenly five things happen at the same time. What should you do?"},{zh:"这五件事是：一、有人敲门；二、电话响了；三、女儿哭起来了；四、外面下大雨，需要关窗户；五、你忘了关水龙头，水不停地流。",py:"Zhè wǔ jiàn shì shì: yī, yǒu rén qiāo mén; èr, diànhuà xiǎng le; sān, nǚ'ér kū qǐlai le; sì, wàimiàn xià dà yǔ, xūyào guān chuānghu; wǔ, nǐ wàngle guān shuǐlóngtóu, shuǐ bùtíng de liú.",en:"The five things are: 1. Someone knocks at the door; 2. The phone rings; 3. Your daughter starts crying; 4. It's raining hard outside and the windows need closing; 5. You forgot to turn off the tap, and the water keeps running."},{zh:"想好了吗？你先选哪个，再选哪个呢？",py:"Xiǎnghǎole ma? Nǐ xiān xuǎn nǎge, zài xuǎn nǎge ne?",en:"Have you decided? Which one do you do first, and which next?"},{zh:"其实，这五件事代表我们生活中的五个方面。敲门的人代表朋友，打电话的人代表男朋友或者女朋友，女儿代表家人，窗户代表工作，水代表钱。",py:"Qíshí, zhè wǔ jiàn shì dàibiǎo wǒmen shēnghuó zhōng de wǔ gè fāngmiàn. Qiāo mén de rén dàibiǎo péngyou, dǎ diànhuà de rén dàibiǎo nánpéngyou huòzhě nǚpéngyou, nǚ'ér dàibiǎo jiārén, chuānghu dàibiǎo gōngzuò, shuǐ dàibiǎo qián.",en:"Actually, these five things stand for five parts of our lives. The person knocking stands for friends, the person calling stands for your boyfriend or girlfriend, your daughter stands for family, the windows stand for work, and the water stands for money."},{zh:"我觉得人更重要！五件事里有三件跟人有关系。其中女儿第一，先照顾她，然后去开门，再接电话。为什么先开门再接电话呢？因为电话可以再打，更容易。另外两件事跟人没有太大关系，所以可以晚点儿做。我先关窗户，再关水龙头。为什么呢？因为虽然水龙头开着会浪费水、浪费钱，但是人更重要。如果窗户开着，孩子会很容易感冒的。",py:"Wǒ juéde rén gèng zhòngyào! Wǔ jiàn shì li yǒu sān jiàn gēn rén yǒu guānxi. Qízhōng nǚ'ér dì-yī, xiān zhàogù tā, ránhòu qù kāi mén, zài jiē diànhuà. Wèishénme xiān kāi mén zài jiē diànhuà ne? Yīnwèi diànhuà kěyǐ zài dǎ, gèng róngyì. Lìngwài liǎng jiàn shì gēn rén méiyǒu tài dà guānxi, suǒyǐ kěyǐ wǎn diǎnr zuò. Wǒ xiān guān chuānghu, zài guān shuǐlóngtóu. Wèishénme ne? Yīnwèi suīrán shuǐlóngtóu kāizhe huì làngfèi shuǐ, làngfèi qián, dànshì rén gèng zhòngyào. Rúguǒ chuānghu kāizhe, háizi huì hěn róngyì gǎnmào de.",en:"I think people matter more! Three of the five things have to do with people. Of those, my daughter comes first — I take care of her first, then I open the door, and then I answer the phone. Why open the door before answering the phone? Because the caller can easily call back. The other two things don't have much to do with people, so they can wait a bit. I'd close the windows first, then turn off the tap. Why? Because although a running tap wastes water and money, people matter more. If the windows are open, the child could easily catch a cold."}],vocab:[{w:"心理",py:"xīnlǐ",pos:"n.",en:"psychology"},{w:"测试",py:"cèshì",pos:"v.",en:"test"},{w:"响",py:"xiǎng",pos:"v.",en:"(of a telephone) ring"},{w:"水龙头",py:"shuǐlóngtóu",pos:"n.",en:"tap, water faucet"},{w:"流",py:"liú",pos:"v.",en:"(of liquid) flow"},{w:"其实",py:"qíshí",pos:"adv.",en:"as a matter of fact"},{w:"照顾",py:"zhàogù",pos:"v.",en:"look after, take care of"},{w:"接",py:"jiē",pos:"v.",en:"pick up (a telephone)"},{w:"浪费",py:"làngfèi",pos:"v.",en:"waste"}],points:[{name:"起来",en:"(indicator of the beginning and continuation of an action)",eg:"女儿哭起来了。",egEn:"Your daughter begins to cry.",zh:"“起来”用在动词后面，表示动作开始，并将继续下去。",enx:"“起来” is used after a verb to indicate that an action starts and will continue.",egs:["（1）大雨下起来了。","（2）上课要迟到了，弟弟赶忙跑了起来。"]},{name:"（一）点儿",en:"a bit, a little",eg:"另外两件事跟人没有太大关系，所以可以晚点儿做。",egEn:"The other two things have little to do with people, so it can be dealt with later.",zh:"“（一）点儿”用在形容词的后面，表示程度轻。",enx:"“（一）点儿” is used after an adjective to indicate “low in degree”.",egs:["（1）天气再热点儿，我们就可以去游泳了。","（2）这个房间小了一点儿，不能放太多东西。"]}],think:["你们觉得“我”的选择怎么样？","你做过别的心理测试吗？能不能说一说？"],tf:[{q:"五件事代表朋友、家人、孩子、工作、金钱。",a:!1},{q:"五件事里面四件事和人有关系。",a:!1},{q:"“我”认为工作最重要。",a:!1},{q:"“我”最后关水龙头，说明“我”喜欢浪费。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"心理学在中国",titleEn:"Psychology in China",zh:"如今，越来越多的中国人意识到：健康包括两个方面，生理健康和心理健康。随着生活节奏的加快和压力的增加，心理健康也受到人们更多的关注。很多大医院都开设了心理门诊，社会上的心理咨询中心、心理咨询热线也纷纷出现，书店里关于心理健康的书籍更是让人眼花缭乱。心理学，已经不再是一门高高在上的学科，而成为了一种与人们的健康和生活息息相关的知识。",en:"More and more Chinese people have become aware that there are two aspects of health, physical and psychological. As life pace speeds up and stresses increase, psychological health has caught much more attention. Many big hospitals have opened psychological sections. Consultancy centres and hotlines addressing psychological problems are emerging in the society. There are numerous books about psychological health in bookstores. Psychology is not an aloof science any longer, but practical knowledge closely related to people’s health and life."}},{n:21,title:"半夜电话",py:"Bànyè diànhuà",en:"A Midnight Call",chars:160,daodu:"如果在半夜，你房间的电话突然响了起来，你会害怕（hàipà：be afraid）吗？",daoduEn:"If the phone in your room suddenly rang in the middle of the night, would you be scared?",paras:[{zh:"半夜里，电话突然响了起来。小李迷迷糊糊地拿起电话，心怦怦直跳，接着他听到：“是你吗，我的孩子？”",py:"Bànyè li, diànhuà tūrán xiǎngle qǐlai. Xiǎo Lǐ mímíhuhu de náqǐ diànhuà, xīn pēngpēng zhí tiào, jiēzhe tā tīngdào: “Shì nǐ ma, wǒ de háizi?”",en:'In the middle of the night, the phone suddenly rang. Half asleep, Xiao Li picked it up, his heart pounding. Then he heard: "Is that you, my child?"'},{zh:"“哦，妈妈，是你。怎么了？”",py:"“Ò, māma, shì nǐ. Zěnme le?”",en:`"Oh, Mom, it's you. What's wrong?"`},{zh:"“没什么。”小李听见了妈妈的笑声。",py:"“Méi shénme.” Xiǎo Lǐ tīngjiànle māma de xiàoshēng.",en:'"Nothing." Xiao Li heard his mom laughing.'},{zh:"“我的孩子，今天是你的生日。”",py:"“Wǒ de háizi, jīntiān shì nǐ de shēngrì.”",en:'"My child, today is your birthday."'},{zh:"“啊？唉，你半夜把我从床上叫起来，就是为了告诉我这件事吗？”",py:"“Á? Ài, nǐ bànyè bǎ wǒ cóng chuáng shang jiào qǐlái, jiù shì wèile gàosu wǒ zhè jiàn shì ma?”",en:'"What? Ugh — you woke me up in the middle of the night just to tell me that?"'},{zh:"“三十年前的今天，你也是在这个时候，把我从床上折腾起来的。”妈妈的一句话把小李逗乐了。",py:"“Sānshí nián qián de jīntiān, nǐ yě shì zài zhège shíhou, bǎ wǒ cóng chuáng shang zhēteng qǐlái de.” Māma de yí jù huà bǎ Xiǎo Lǐ dòulè le.",en:`"Thirty years ago today, at this very hour, you got me out of bed too!" His mom's words made Xiao Li laugh.`},{zh:"对于孩子的生日，记得最清楚的人也许不是孩子自己，而是他的母亲。",py:"Duìyú háizi de shēngrì, jì de zuì qīngchu de rén yěxǔ bú shì háizi zìjǐ, ér shì tā de mǔqīn.",en:"When it comes to a child's birthday, the person who remembers it best may not be the child, but the mother."}],vocab:[{w:"半夜",py:"bànyè",pos:"n.",en:"midnight"},{w:"怦",py:"pēng",pos:"onomatopoeia",en:"(of the heart) thump, pound"},{w:"接着",py:"jiēzhe",pos:"adv.",en:"then, afterwards"},{w:"折腾",py:"zhēteng",pos:"v.",en:"torture, torment"},{w:"逗乐",py:"dòulè",pos:"",en:"amuse, tickle"},{w:"对于",py:"duìyú",pos:"prep.",en:"with regard to"}],points:[{name:"迷迷糊糊",en:"dazed",eg:"小李迷迷糊糊地拿起电话。",egEn:"Xiao Li picked up the phone in a daze.",zh:"“迷糊”，形容词。双音节形容词的重叠形式一般是 AABB 式。形容词重叠后，描写作用更强。",enx:"“迷糊” is an adjective. Some double-syllable adjectives follow the reduplication pattern of AABB, which can make the description more expressive.",egs:["（1）看到妹妹快快乐乐的样子，我也笑了起来。","（2）为了漂漂亮亮地过年，很多女孩儿都买了新衣服。"]},{name:"告诉我这件事",en:"tell me this",eg:"你半夜把我从床上叫起来，就是为了告诉我这件事吗？",egEn:"You woke me up in the middle of the night just to tell me this?",zh:"有些动词，比如“告诉”、“通知”、“给”、“送”、“交”、“教”等，可以带两个宾语，一个指人，一个指物。指人的宾语放在指物的宾语前面。",enx:"Some verbs in Chinese, such as “告诉”, “通知”, “给”, “送”, “交”, “教” and so on, can have two objects. One refers to a person, and the other refers to something, which is usually put after the person.",egs:["（1）李老师教我们汉语。","（2）王太太给小儿子两个苹果。"]}],think:["半夜里发生了什么事？","你觉得一个人的生日谁记得最清楚？","你会记住谁的生日？为什么？"],tf:[{q:"接到电话，小李的心怦怦直跳，因为他还没有睡醒。",a:!1},{q:"小李是在半夜出生的。",a:!0},{q:"妈妈给小李打电话，就是为了告诉他今天是他的生日。",a:!0},{q:"小李今年三十岁了。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"孩子的生日，母亲的难日",titleEn:"Children's Birthday Is Mothers' Suffering Day",zh:"中国有句俗话，叫“孩子的生日，母亲的难日”。意思就是生孩子对母亲来说是一件十分痛苦的事情。其实，不仅是生孩子这一天，“怀胎十月”，妈妈哪一天不是小心翼翼地度过？所以，中国人过生日的时候一般都要和母亲一起庆祝，以表达对母亲的感谢。",en:"There is a Chinese saying, “Children's birthday is mothers' suffering day.” It means that it is quite painful for a mother to give birth to a child. As a matter of fact, delivery is not the only suffering, each day of the “ten-month pregnancy” is spent in discomfort and concern. Thus, when celebrating their birthday, a Chinese child generally spends it with his/her mother to express his/her gratitude."}},{n:22,title:"恋爱日记",py:"Liàn'ài rìjì",en:"A Diary of Her Love",chars:280,daodu:"你喜欢旅游吗？旅游的时候遇到过有趣的事情吗？一起来看看一个女孩儿在旅行中的故事吧。",daoduEn:"Do you like traveling? Has anything funny ever happened to you on a trip? Let's read a girl's story from her trip.",paras:[{zh:"一个漂亮的女孩儿坐船去旅游。她有写日记的习惯，让我们来看看她的旅行日记吧。",py:"Yí gè piàoliang de nǚháir zuò chuán qù lǚyóu. Tā yǒu xiě rìjì de xíguàn, ràng wǒmen lái kànkan tā de lǚxíng rìjì ba.",en:"A pretty girl went on a trip by ship. She liked to keep a diary, so let's take a look at her travel diary."},{zh:"第一天：我认识了船长，他个子高高的，头发黑黑的，眼睛大大的。他长得真帅！",py:"Dì-yī tiān: Wǒ rènshile chuánzhǎng, tā gèzi gāogāo de, tóufa hēihēi de, yǎnjing dàdà de. Tā zhǎng de zhēn shuài!",en:"Day 1: I met the captain. He's tall, with black hair and big eyes. He's so handsome!"},{zh:"第二天：船长请我和他一起吃晚饭。他又热情又有礼貌，说话也很有趣，还给我讲了很多笑话。我却像个傻瓜一样，一句话也说不出来。",py:"Dì-èr tiān: Chuánzhǎng qǐng wǒ hé tā yìqǐ chī wǎnfàn. Tā yòu rèqíng yòu yǒu lǐmào, shuōhuà yě hěn yǒuqù, hái gěi wǒ jiǎngle hěn duō xiàohua. Wǒ què xiàng gè shǎguā yíyàng, yí jù huà yě shuō bù chūlái.",en:"Day 2: The captain invited me to have dinner with him. He's warm and polite, he's fun to talk to, and he told me lots of jokes. But I was like a fool — I couldn't say a single word."},{zh:"第三天：船长带我在船上到处参观，还请我去了他的办公室。他一直深情地看着我，可惜办公室里还有其他人。",py:"Dì-sān tiān: Chuánzhǎng dài wǒ zài chuán shang dàochù cānguān, hái qǐng wǒ qùle tā de bàngōngshì. Tā yìzhí shēnqíng de kànzhe wǒ, kěxī bàngōngshì li hái yǒu qítā rén.",en:"Day 3: The captain showed me all around the ship and invited me to his office. He kept gazing at me lovingly. Too bad there were other people in the office."},{zh:"第四天：船长再次请我吃饭，我们还喝了点儿酒。后来我们一起去了他的房间。他说他爱我，要和我结婚。虽然我也喜欢他，可是我觉得这一切太快了，我还没准备好呢。于是我告诉他，我要再想想。",py:"Dì-sì tiān: Chuánzhǎng zàicì qǐng wǒ chīfàn, wǒmen hái hēle diǎnr jiǔ. Hòulái wǒmen yìqǐ qùle tā de fángjiān. Tā shuō tā ài wǒ, yào hé wǒ jiéhūn. Suīrán wǒ yě xǐhuan tā, kěshì wǒ juéde zhè yíqiè tài kuài le, wǒ hái méi zhǔnbèi hǎo ne. Yúshì wǒ gàosu tā, wǒ yào zài xiǎngxiang.",en:"Day 4: The captain invited me to dinner again, and we had a little wine. Later we went to his cabin together. He said he loved me and wanted to marry me. I like him too, but I felt it was all happening too fast — I wasn't ready yet. So I told him I needed to think about it."},{zh:"第五天：他又说要和我结婚，还笑着说如果我不愿意，他就把船撞到冰山上。",py:"Dì-wǔ tiān: Tā yòu shuō yào hé wǒ jiéhūn, hái xiàozhe shuō rúguǒ wǒ bú yuànyì, tā jiù bǎ chuán zhuàngdào bīngshān shang.",en:"Day 5: He asked me to marry him again, and said with a smile that if I said no, he would crash the ship into an iceberg."},{zh:"第六天：我救了船上所有的人。",py:"Dì-liù tiān: Wǒ jiùle chuán shang suǒyǒu de rén.",en:"Day 6: I saved everyone on the ship."}],vocab:[{w:"船",py:"chuán",pos:"n.",en:"ship"},{w:"个子",py:"gèzi",pos:"n.",en:"height, stature"},{w:"头发",py:"tóufa",pos:"n.",en:"hair (on the human head)"},{w:"帅",py:"shuài",pos:"adj.",en:"handsome"},{w:"傻瓜",py:"shǎguā",pos:"n.",en:"fool"},{w:"深情",py:"shēnqíng",pos:"adj.",en:"affectionate"},{w:"一切",py:"yíqiè",pos:"pron.",en:"all"},{w:"救",py:"jiù",pos:"v.",en:"save"}],points:[{name:"参观",en:"visit",eg:"船长带我在船上到处参观。",egEn:"The captain showed me around the ship.",zh:"“参观”，动词。是“到某一个地方看、观察”的意思。",enx:"“参观” is a verb that means “to make a visit”.",egs:["（1）我们一到北京，老师就带我们参观了这个学校。","（2）听说你的家很漂亮，我可以参观一下吗？"]},{name:"可惜",en:"regrettable",eg:"他一直深情地看着我，可惜办公室里还有其他人。",egEn:"He was watching me affectionately; unfortunately, there were other people in the office.",zh:"“可惜”，形容词。是“让人觉得遗憾”的意思。",enx:"“可惜” is an adjective with the meaning of “feeling sorry because of unpleasant results”.",egs:["（1）她很喜欢那件衣服，可惜太贵了。","（2）我们都没有去北京看奥运会，太可惜了！"]},{name:"准备",en:"prepare",eg:"我觉得这一切太快了，我还没准备好呢。",egEn:"I felt all of those things had happened too fast, and I had not prepared.",zh:"“准备”，动词。表示开始做某事之前预先安排。",enx:"“准备” is a verb that means “to get ready beforehand”.",egs:["（1）新年快到了，全家人都在忙着准备新年的礼物。","（2）我回到家的时候，妈妈已经准备好了饭菜。"]}],think:["女孩儿喜欢船长吗？","“办公室里还有其他人”，女孩儿为什么觉得可惜？","故事的结果是什么？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"船长（　）。",options:["个子不高，头发黄黄的","不爱说话","个子高高的，长得很帅","不喜欢讲笑话"],answer:2},{q:"“我”没有马上同意和船长结婚，是因为（　）。",options:["我觉得一切太快了","我不喜欢船长","船长长得不帅","船长没有礼貌"],answer:0},{q:"“我救了船上所有的人”的意思是（　）。",options:["我同意和船长结婚了","船撞到了冰山上","我不愿意和船长结婚","我会游泳"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"郑和下西洋",titleEn:"Zheng He's Voyages to the Western Seas",zh:"郑和是中国历史上伟大的航海家。公元1405年7月11日，郑和奉明成祖朱棣之命，出使中国南海以西的国家和地区，称为“下西洋”。郑和第一次下西洋比哥伦布发现美洲新大陆早87年，比达·伽马经过好望角早92年，比麦哲伦环球航行早114年。在1405～1433年的28年间，郑和率领船队七下西洋，打通并拓展了中国与亚非三十多个国家和地区的海上交通，为世界航海事业的发展和各国人民的交流做出了不可磨灭的贡献。",en:"Zheng He was a great voyager in the history of China. On July 11th, 1405, he was sent on a diplomatic mission by Emperor Zhu Di of Ming Dynasty to countries and areas west to the South China Sea, known as “to the Western Seas”. His first voyage to the Western Seas was 87 years earlier than Columbus' discovery of the New Continent of America, 92 years before Vasco da Gama's sailing to the Hope Cape, and 114 years prior to Magellan's sailing around the world. During the 28 years from 1405 to 1433, Zheng He with his team had sailed to the Western Seas seven times, starting and extending ocean navigation lines between China and over 30 countries and areas in Asia and Africa. His voyages are an indelible contribution to the development of seafaring and communication between different peoples."}},{n:23,title:"伤心的故事",py:"Shāngxīn de gùshi",en:"A Sad Story",chars:248,daodu:"三个好朋友住在饭店的三十五层。电梯坏了，只好一起爬楼梯。大家一边爬，一边讲笑话、唱歌，最后一个人讲了个故事……",daoduEn:"Three good friends are staying on the 35th floor of a hotel. The elevator is broken, so they have to climb the stairs together. As they climb, they tell jokes and sing songs, and at last one of them tells a story...",paras:[{zh:"有三个人到南京旅游，他们住在一个饭店的三十五层。晚上他们一起出去看电影，回来的时候已经很晚了。糟糕的是，所有的电梯都坏了，他们只好自己走上去。",py:"Yǒu sān gè rén dào Nánjīng lǚyóu, tāmen zhù zài yí gè fàndiàn de sānshíwǔ céng. Wǎnshang tāmen yìqǐ chūqù kàn diànyǐng, huílái de shíhou yǐjīng hěn wǎn le. Zāogāo de shì, suǒyǒu de diàntī dōu huài le, tāmen zhǐhǎo zìjǐ zǒu shàngqu.",en:"Three people went on a trip to Nanjing. They stayed on the 35th floor of a hotel. One evening they went out to see a movie, and it was very late when they got back. Worse still, all the elevators were broken, so they had to walk up."},{zh:"他们开始爬楼梯。一个人说：“我们这样走太无聊了。这样吧，我们一个人讲笑话，一个人唱歌，一个人讲故事。”",py:"Tāmen kāishǐ pá lóutī. Yí gè rén shuō: “Wǒmen zhèyàng zǒu tài wúliáo le. Zhèyàng ba, wǒmen yí gè rén jiǎng xiàohua, yí gè rén chànggē, yí gè rén jiǎng gùshi.”",en:'They started climbing the stairs. One of them said, "Walking like this is so boring. How about this: one of us tells jokes, one sings songs, and one tells a story."'},{zh:"大家都觉得很好。他们继续爬楼梯，一个人讲了笑话，然后第二个人唱了歌。到二十五层的时候，大家都累了，决定先休息一下。",py:"Dàjiā dōu juéde hěn hǎo. Tāmen jìxù pá lóutī, yí gè rén jiǎngle xiàohua, ránhòu dì-èr gè rén chàngle gē. Dào èrshíwǔ céng de shíhou, dàjiā dōu lèi le, juédìng xiān xiūxi yíxià.",en:"Everyone thought that was a good idea. They kept climbing. One of them told jokes, and then the second sang songs. By the 25th floor, they were all tired and decided to take a rest."},{zh:"讲笑话的人对第三个人说：“我讲了笑话，他唱了歌，现在该你讲故事了。你要讲一个长一点儿的故事，最好有一个伤心的结尾。”",py:"Jiǎng xiàohua de rén duì dì-sān gè rén shuō: “Wǒ jiǎngle xiàohua, tā chàngle gē, xiànzài gāi nǐ jiǎng gùshi le. Nǐ yào jiǎng yí gè cháng yìdiǎnr de gùshi, zuìhǎo yǒu yí gè shāngxīn de jiéwěi.”",en:`The one who had told jokes said to the third, "I told jokes, he sang songs — now it's your turn to tell a story. Make it a longer one, and it'd be best if it had a sad ending."`},{zh:"第三个人说：“我现在就讲一个伤心的故事，故事不长，但很让人伤心——我们的房间钥匙忘在一楼服务台了。”",py:"Dì-sān gè rén shuō: “Wǒ xiànzài jiù jiǎng yí gè shāngxīn de gùshi, gùshi bù cháng, dàn hěn ràng rén shāngxīn — wǒmen de fángjiān yàoshi wàng zài yī lóu fúwùtái le.”",en:`The third said, "I'll tell you a sad story right now. It's not long, but it's very sad: we left our room key at the front desk on the first floor."`}],vocab:[{w:"糟糕",py:"zāogāo",pos:"adj.",en:"bad, terrible"},{w:"电梯",py:"diàntī",pos:"n.",en:"lift"},{w:"楼梯",py:"lóutī",pos:"n.",en:"stairs"},{w:"无聊",py:"wúliáo",pos:"adj.",en:"boring"},{w:"休息",py:"xiūxi",pos:"v.",en:"rest"},{w:"结尾",py:"jiéwěi",pos:"n.",en:"ending"},{w:"钥匙",py:"yàoshi",pos:"n.",en:"key"},{w:"服务台",py:"fúwùtái",pos:"n.",en:"service counter"}],points:[{name:"一下",en:"for a short while, have a try",eg:"到二十五层的时候，大家都累了，决定先休息一下。",egEn:"Having reached the 25th floor, everybody felt exhausted, and decided to have a rest.",zh:"“一下”，放在动词后面，表示动作持续时间短或试着做。",enx:"“一下” is usually put after a verb to indicate “for a short while” or “have a try”.",egs:["（1）下课的时候应该出去活动一下，休息休息。","（2）你敲一下门，看看里面有没有人。"]},{name:"该",en:"it is one's turn to …",eg:"我讲了笑话，他唱了歌，现在该你讲故事了。",egEn:"I have told a joke, he has sung a song, and now it is your turn to tell a story.",zh:"“该”，动词。表示应该轮到某人做某事。后面常加“了”，但否定的时候一般不加。",enx:"“该” is a verb that means “it is one's turn to do something”. It is usually used before “了”. But there is no “了” in a negative sentence.",egs:["（1）五点了，该放学了。","（2）今天不该他休息，他怎么没来上班？"]},{name:"最好",en:"had better",eg:"你要讲一个长一点儿的故事，最好有一个伤心的结尾。",egEn:"You are supposed to tell a story a little bit long, and you had better give it a sad ending.",zh:"“最好”，副词。常常表示建议。",enx:"“最好” is an adverb usually used to give a suggestion.",egs:["（1）为了你的健康，你最好少吸烟。","（2）今天天气很冷，你最好多穿一点儿。"]}],think:["他们三个人住在哪层楼？","他们为什么要爬楼梯？","故事的结尾让人伤心吗？"],tf:[{q:"这三个人住在上海一家饭店的三十五层。",a:!1},{q:"走到十五层的时候，大家决定休息一下。",a:!1},{q:"第三个人讲完故事后，才发现没带钥匙。",a:!1}],mc:[],tip:{title:"“马大哈”的由来",titleEn:"The Origin of “马大哈”",zh:"“马大哈”是指做事马马虎虎的人。这个词来自于相声《买猴》。一位叫“马大哈”的干部，以马虎出名。他写了个购货单，本来要通知“到天津市的东北角，买猴牌肥皂五十箱”，可是错写成了“到东北买猴五十只”。结果，采购员跑遍了大半个中国去采购猴子。猴子运回来以后，群猴出笼大闹百货公司……",en:"The term “马大哈” refers to those who are careless about their work or life. It was coined from a comic Chinese cross talk called Buying Monkeys. Ma Daha, a manager of a department store, was well known for his carelessness. He made a shopping list with the intention of having his purchasing man “go to the northeast corner of Tianjin and buy 50 boxes of Monkey-brand soap”. However, he wrote by mistake the list as, “Go to the Northeast and buy 50 monkeys”. As a result, the purchasing man travelled across half of the country to buy monkeys. When the 50 monkeys were brought in, they all escaped from the cages and raised hell in the store ..."}},{n:24,title:"最好的消息",py:"Zuì hǎo de xiāoxi",en:"The Best News",chars:285,daodu:"如果你知道一个人欺骗（qīpiàn：deceive）了你，你会不会生气？",daoduEn:"If you found out someone had tricked you, would you get angry?",paras:[{zh:"一个著名的运动员赢了一场重要的比赛，得到了很多奖金。比赛结束后，他准备回家。这时候，一个年轻的女子向他走来。她先向运动员表示祝贺，然后就告诉他，她可怜的孩子病得很重，也许会死，而她却没钱给他看病。",py:"Yí gè zhùmíng de yùndòngyuán yíngle yí chǎng zhòngyào de bǐsài, dédàole hěn duō jiǎngjīn. Bǐsài jiéshù hòu, tā zhǔnbèi huíjiā. Zhè shíhou, yí gè niánqīng de nǚzǐ xiàng tā zǒulái. Tā xiān xiàng yùndòngyuán biǎoshì zhùhè, ránhòu jiù gàosu tā, tā kělián de háizi bìng de hěn zhòng, yěxǔ huì sǐ, ér tā què méi qián gěi tā kànbìng.",en:"A famous athlete won an important competition and received a lot of prize money. After the competition, he was getting ready to go home. Just then, a young woman came up to him. First she congratulated him, and then she told him that her poor child was very sick and might die, but she had no money to pay the doctor."},{zh:"运动员被她的话深深地感动了。他想了想，拿出笔在刚赢得的支票上飞快地签了名，然后把支票给了那个女子。",py:"Yùndòngyuán bèi tā de huà shēnshēn de gǎndòng le. Tā xiǎngle xiǎng, náchū bǐ zài gāng yíngdé de zhīpiào shang fēikuài de qiānle míng, ránhòu bǎ zhīpiào gěile nàge nǚzǐ.",en:"The athlete was deeply moved by her words. After thinking for a moment, he took out a pen, quickly signed the check he had just won, and gave it to the woman."},{zh:"“这是比赛奖金。祝可怜的孩子好运。”他说。",py:"“Zhè shì bǐsài jiǎngjīn. Zhù kělián de háizi hǎoyùn.” Tā shuō.",en:'"This is the prize money. I hope your poor child has good luck," he said.'},{zh:"一个星期后，运动员正在一家饭店吃饭。饭店老板问他，一周前是不是遇到过一个年轻女子，说自己的孩子病得很重。",py:"Yí gè xīngqī hòu, yùndòngyuán zhèngzài yì jiā fàndiàn chīfàn. Fàndiàn lǎobǎn wèn tā, yì zhōu qián shì bú shì yùdàoguo yí gè niánqīng nǚzǐ, shuō zìjǐ de háizi bìng de hěn zhòng.",en:"A week later, the athlete was eating at a restaurant. The owner asked him whether, a week ago, he had met a young woman who said her child was very sick."},{zh:"他点了点头。",py:"Tā diǎnle diǎn tóu.",en:"He nodded."},{zh:"“哦，对你来说这是个坏消息。”老板说，“那个女人是个骗子，她根本就没有什么病得很重的孩子。她还没有结婚呢！”",py:"“Ò, duì nǐ lái shuō zhè shì gè huài xiāoxi.” Lǎobǎn shuō, “Nàge nǚrén shì gè piànzi, tā gēnběn jiù méiyǒu shénme bìng de hěn zhòng de háizi. Tā hái méiyǒu jiéhūn ne!”",en:`"Oh, I'm afraid this is bad news for you," the owner said. "That woman is a cheat. She doesn't have any sick child at all. She isn't even married!"`},{zh:"“你是说根本就没有一个小孩子病得快死了？”",py:"“Nǐ shì shuō gēnběn jiù méiyǒu yí gè xiǎo háizi bìng de kuài sǐ le?”",en:`"You mean there's no little child who's so sick he's about to die?"`},{zh:"“是这样的，根本就没有。”",py:"“Shì zhèyàng de, gēnběn jiù méiyǒu.”",en:`"That's right. There isn't one at all."`},{zh:"“是吗？这真是我听到的最好的消息！”",py:"“Shì ma? Zhè zhēn shì wǒ tīngdào de zuì hǎo de xiāoxi!”",en:`"Really? That's the best news I've ever heard!"`}],vocab:[{w:"赢",py:"yíng",pos:"v.",en:"win"},{w:"比赛",py:"bǐsài",pos:"n.",en:"game, match"},{w:"可怜",py:"kělián",pos:"adj.",en:"poor"},{w:"感动",py:"gǎndòng",pos:"v.",en:"move"},{w:"签",py:"qiān",pos:"v.",en:"sign (one's name)"},{w:"好运",py:"hǎoyùn",pos:"n.",en:"fortune"},{w:"消息",py:"xiāoxi",pos:"n.",en:"news"},{w:"骗子",py:"piànzi",pos:"n.",en:"cheater"}],points:[{name:"祝贺",en:"congratulate",eg:"她先向运动员表示祝贺，然后就说她可怜的孩子病得很重。",egEn:"First she congratulated the sportsman, and then told him that her poor child was seriously ill.",zh:"“祝贺”，动词。表示在对方取得成功或有喜事时，用语言向对方表示庆祝。",enx:"“祝贺” is a verb that means “to express congratulations in words” when someone has achieved success or something nice has happened.",egs:["（1）我生日的时候，很多同学向我表示祝贺。","（2）祝贺你这次考试取得了第一名！"]},{name:"祝",en:"wish",eg:"祝可怜的孩子好运。",egEn:"Wish the poor child good luck.",zh:"“祝”，动词。表示对人或事情表达良好的愿望。",enx:"“祝” is a verb used to express good wishes to somebody or something.",egs:["（1）马上就要出发了，祝你们一路平安！","（2）祝你生日快乐！"]}],think:["那个年轻的女子想干什么？","那个孩子的病好了吗？","你觉得这个运动员傻不傻？你喜欢他吗？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"运动员在支票上签了名，是因为（　）。",options:["那个女子想要他的签名","他想给那个女子写信","他想把奖金送给那个女子","饭店老板让他签名"],answer:2},{q:"运动员把比赛的奖金送给女子，因为（　）。",options:["他觉得奖金太少了","他被女子的话感动了","那个女子是他的朋友","他不需要这些钱"],answer:1},{q:"那个女子是个骗子，运动员却觉得这是个好消息，因为（　）。",options:["他可以要回奖金了","那个女子还没有结婚","他不喜欢那个女子","没有一个孩子病得快死了"],answer:3}],tip:{title:"名人的慈善行动",titleEn:"Celebrities' Charity Actions",zh:"现在，越来越多的中国企业家和明星开始具有了慈善意识。这不是一个简单的时尚行为。慈善事业既有利于树立他们自身良好的形象，也会有利于一些企业家事业的发展，而且更重要的是，这样做能够让普通人多一些慈善意识。2008年5月12日中国四川省发生大地震后，功夫明星李连杰发起的“中国红十字会李连杰壹基金计划”就和很多普通人一起，共同努力，给灾区人民送去了很多帮助。",en:"Nowadays, more and more entrepreneurs and stars in China have become aware of the importance of charity. It is not just a behavior of fad, but a cause that helps to establish a favorable public image of these entrepreneurs and stars, which, in turn, helps their career development. Their examples also help to promote charity awareness among the general public. After the 5.12 Earthquake in Sichuan, Jet Li (Li Lianjie), a famous kongfu star, initiated “Red Cross Society of China Jet Li One Foundation Project” and mobilized many people to work together with him in the relief efforts to help earthquake victims."}},{n:25,title:"钱越多就越快乐吗？",py:"Qián yuè duō jiù yuè kuàilè ma?",en:"More Money, More Happiness?",chars:226,daodu:"你每天都很快乐吗？你觉得什么会影响一个人的快乐呢？钱、健康，还是别的？",daoduEn:"Are you happy every day? What do you think affects a person's happiness — money, health, or something else?",paras:[{zh:"钱越多就越快乐吗？一般认为，富国的人比穷国的人更快乐。但新的研究认为，钱对人们生活的影响是有限的。",py:"Qián yuè duō jiù yuè kuàilè ma? Yìbān rènwéi, fù guó de rén bǐ qióng guó de rén gèng kuàilè. Dàn xīn de yánjiū rènwéi, qián duì rénmen shēnghuó de yǐngxiǎng shì yǒuxiàn de.",en:"Does more money mean more happiness? People generally believe that people in rich countries are happier than people in poor countries. But new research suggests that money has only a limited effect on people's lives."},{zh:"人均年收入不到一万美元的国家，一般是收入越高的人，快乐的时间就越长。而收入一万美元以上的国家，人们的收入和快乐的时间就没什么关系了。",py:"Rénjūn niánshōurù bú dào yíwàn měiyuán de guójiā, yìbān shì shōurù yuè gāo de rén, kuàilè de shíjiān jiù yuè cháng. Ér shōurù yíwàn měiyuán yǐshàng de guójiā, rénmen de shōurù hé kuàilè de shíjiān jiù méi shénme guānxi le.",en:"In countries where the average yearly income is under 10,000 US dollars, generally the higher people's income, the longer they feel happy. But in countries where income is over 10,000 dollars, there's not much connection between people's income and how long they feel happy."},{zh:"社会学家们还发现，一个国家越自由，这个国家的人就越快乐。比如说，生活在这个国家的孩子能不能获得更大的独立性；生活在这个国家的人能不能获得更多的信息；生活在这个国家的妇女能不能受到更好的教育，做更多的工作，有更高的收入。如果能够做到这些，那么人们快乐的时间就会增加。",py:"Shèhuìxuéjiāmen hái fāxiàn, yí gè guójiā yuè zìyóu, zhège guójiā de rén jiù yuè kuàilè. Bǐrúshuō, shēnghuó zài zhège guójiā de háizi néng bù néng huòdé gèng dà de dúlìxìng; shēnghuó zài zhège guójiā de rén néng bù néng huòdé gèng duō de xìnxī; shēnghuó zài zhège guójiā de fùnǚ néng bù néng shòudào gèng hǎo de jiàoyù, zuò gèng duō de gōngzuò, yǒu gèng gāo de shōurù. Rúguǒ nénggòu zuòdào zhèxiē, nàme rénmen kuàilè de shíjiān jiù huì zēngjiā.",en:"Sociologists have also found that the freer a country is, the happier its people are. For example: can children in that country become more independent? Can people there get more information? Can women there get a better education, do more kinds of work and earn more? If all this can be done, people will spend more of their time feeling happy."}],vocab:[{w:"研究",py:"yánjiū",pos:"v.",en:"research"},{w:"收入",py:"shōurù",pos:"n.",en:"income"},{w:"社会学家",py:"shèhuìxuéjiā",pos:"n.",en:"sociologist"},{w:"自由",py:"zìyóu",pos:"adj.",en:"free, liberal"},{w:"独立性",py:"dúlìxìng",pos:"n.",en:"independency"},{w:"信息",py:"xìnxī",pos:"n.",en:"information"}],points:[{name:"有限",en:"limited",eg:"但新的研究认为，钱对人们生活的影响是有限的。",egEn:"But a latest research reveals that money has limited influence on people's life.",zh:"“有限”，形容词。表示数量不多或程度不高。",enx:"“有限” is an adjective with the meaning of “not very great in amount, number or degree”.",egs:["（1）我的汉语水平有限，许多句子都听不懂。","（2）由于在北京的时间有限，我们没有能去长城。"]},{name:"以上",en:"above, over",eg:"而收入一万美元以上的国家，人们的收入和快乐的时间就没什么关系了。",egEn:"But in those countries, where the average income is over ten thousand dollars, income has little to do with the length of happy time.",zh:"“以上”，名词。和“以下”相对，表示次序、数目、位置等在某一个点上面。",enx:"“以上” is a noun opposite in meaning to “以下”, and it indicates something precedes something else in an order, more than it in amount or above it in terms of location.",egs:["（1）这个商场的三楼以上是饭馆。","（2）在中国，一米一以上的小孩儿坐公共汽车需要买票。"]}],think:["富国的人比穷国的人更快乐吗？","“钱对人们生活的影响是有限的”是什么意思？"],tf:[],mc:[{q:"人均年收入在一万美元以上的国家，人们（　）。",options:["收入越高，就越快乐","收入越高，快乐的时间越短","都非常快乐","收入和快乐的时间没什么关系"],answer:3},{q:"社会学家发现，一个国家越（　），这个国家的人就越快乐。",options:["富","自由","大","安静"],answer:1},{q:"这篇文章认为，钱对人们的快乐（　）。",options:["没有影响","影响最大","影响是有限的","影响越来越大"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"你幸福吗？",titleEn:"Are You Happy?",zh:"曾经有一个中国的摄影师展览过这么一组作品，名字就叫《你幸福吗？》。他的拍摄对象涉及社会各阶层的人，有贩夫走卒，也有亿万富翁。拍摄之前，他先和对方寒暄一阵，待熟悉之后，突然问一句“你觉得你幸福吗”，然后抓拍对方听到问题后一刹那的表情。事实证明，大家的表情各种各样，而最多的是一种处于思考中的迷茫。可见，对于大多数中国人来说，是否幸福与金钱无关。",en:"Once there was a Chinese photographer who exhibited his series of photos, called Are You Happy?. He photographed people at all levels of society, from peddlers to billionaires. Before taking pictures, he would have a small talk with them for a while. When acquainted, he would ask them abruptly, “Are you happy?” Then, he would snapshot their expressions the moment they heard the question. It is true that the expressions vary from one to another. Most of them were pondering and puzzled. It showed that happiness has nothing to do with money for most Chinese people."}}],s={key:e,title:n,titleEn:i,series:t,seriesEn:h,level:o,lessons:a};export{s as default,e as key,a as lessons,o as level,t as series,h as seriesEn,n as title,i as titleEn};
